sk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stanley Reed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f652b209-a4b5-5091-8a5e-5bef1c7ddb08', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f652b209-a4b5-5091-8a5e-5bef1c7ddb08'}, {'abstract': 'The ability to bounce back is more important now than ever; here’s how to impart it', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/parenting/raising-resilient-kids.html', 'snippet': 'The ability to bounce back is more important now than ever; here’s how to impart it', 'lead_paragraph': 'In my early teens, my dad took myself, my best friend and our neighbor on a grueling backpacking trip connecting California’s Yosemite Valley to Half Dome to nearby Clouds Rest mountain and back again.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/well/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/01/well/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/well/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/well/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1166, 'width': 1750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/well/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/01/well/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/well/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS/1NL-PAR-RESILIENCY-KIDS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Secret to Raising a Resilient Kid', 'kicker': 'The NYT Parenting Newsletter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Here to Help; How to Raise a Resilient Kid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'audio-positive-happy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'audio-neutral-informative', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-01T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Parenting', 'section_name': 'Parenting', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Vance', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vance', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cea34d6-cf79-5cc7-8e6a-a93424dc9bde', 'word_count': 1203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cea34d6-cf79-5cc7-8e6a-a93424dc9bde'}, {'abstract': 'One boy’s violent act of retribution raises uncomfortable questions about the world we’ve made for children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/magazine/tiktok-pranks.html', 'snippet': 'One boy’s violent act of retribution raises uncomfortable questions about the world we’ve made for children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was a kid, one of my plans was to appear on some kind of candid video show. I was dimly aware of “Candid Camera” as a phenomenon of my parents’ or possibly my grandparents’ generation, but I fantasized about “America’s Funniest Home Videos,” or even just a spot on the local news. In addition to making me famous, this appearance would capture my insouciant charm. As an unusually self-conscious child — one who used the word “insouciant” a lot, if that gives you a sense of the problem — I hoped a candid video might show me as I really was: likable, quick-thinking, maybe possessed of some undiscovered athletic ability. The best part of this plan was that I could do nothing to advance it; by definition, I had to wait for the camera to discover me. I knew the odds of such a thing happening were astronomical. In the 1990s, people did not just roll up and shoot video of children on the street.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05Mag-Screenland-1/05Mag-Screenland-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05Mag-Screenland-1/05Mag-Screenland-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05Mag-Screenland-1/05Mag-Screenland-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05Mag-Screenland-1/05Mag-Screenland-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1220, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05Mag-Screenland-1/05Mag-Screenland-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05Mag-Screenland-1/05Mag-Screenland-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05Mag-Screenland-1/05Mag-Screenland-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Far Can You Go to Resist Being the Subject of a Viral Video?', 'kicker': 'Screenland', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lights Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'TikTok (ByteDance)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-01T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25ad2711-a184-5a18-b3d4-fa6034986a39', 'word_count': 1212, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25ad2711-a184-5a18-b3d4-fa6034986a39'}, {'abstract': 'It’s the simplest recipe: a little bit braised and a little bit roasted in a covered Dutch oven.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/magazine/chicken-in-a-pot-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'It’s the simplest recipe: a little bit braised and a little bit roasted in a covered Dutch oven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometime in my early 20s, I went to Paris to strengthen my French and my character. I’m not sure what prompted this — probably something I read — but I woke up one morning and realized that I’d never lived alone. I’d lived with my parents, had roommates briefly and then married when I was 19. All of a sudden this seemed like a shortcoming in need of immediate attention. And so I took all the vacation time I had coming to me from work, booked the cheapest flight I could find, got a tiny top-floor room in a small hotel and enrolled in a course at the Sorbonne. It didn’t take long to discover that going to the movies was a better way to learn a language than sitting in a classroom, and that for me, living alone made me lonely. I’m certain that’s why I followed a stranger home for dinner.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-eat/05mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-eat/05mag-eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-eat/05mag-eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-eat/05mag-eat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1542, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-eat/05mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-eat/05mag-eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-eat/05mag-eat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Holy-Grail, One-Pot Roast Chicken', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chicken in Every Pot: A simple dish learned in Paris turns out to be timeless.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-01T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorie Greenspan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenspan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/59ef99b2-b48d-52c4-8983-f77cb1e7cae2', 'word_count': 1035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/59ef99b2-b48d-52c4-8983-f77cb1e7cae2'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes, what’s most important becomes clear only with the passage of time.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/opinion/covid-summer.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes, what’s most important becomes clear only with the passage of time.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our order was ready. I headed to the counter and retrieved the fried seafood platter for two, a pornographic avalanche of crispy calamari, shrimp, scallops. There were whole belly clams. There were oysters and codfish, and a mountain of onion rings. There were French fries and homemade coleslaw, and ketchup. There was tartar sauce.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/opinion/01Boylan-V2/01Boylan-V2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/05/opinion/01Boylan-V2/01Boylan-V2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/opinion/01Boylan-V2/01Boylan-V2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/opinion/01Boylan-V2/01Boylan-V2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/opinion/01Boylan-V2/01Boylan-V2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/05/opinion/01Boylan-V2/01Boylan-V2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/opinion/01Boylan-V2/01Boylan-V2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Never Knew How Golden My Summers Were', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headl