ct', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disease Rates', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-01T09:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ad8ce5d-458f-508a-8024-1ba0749d9fde', 'word_count': 1334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ad8ce5d-458f-508a-8024-1ba0749d9fde'}, {'abstract': 'As Republicans continue to challenge the 2020 results, voting equipment is being compromised when partisan insiders and unvetted operatives gain access.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/us/politics/gop-us-election-security.html', 'snippet': 'As Republicans continue to challenge the 2020 results, voting equipment is being compromised when partisan insiders and unvetted operatives gain access.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late one night in May, after surveillance cameras had inexplicably been turned off, three people entered the secure area of a warehouse in Mesa County, Colo., where crucial election equipment was stored. They copied hard drives and election-management software from voting machines, the authorities said, and then fled.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/us/00election-security1/merlin_187180638_e065f7f1-2373-4db7-ab57-6d40d699d35b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/08/20/us/00election-security1/merlin_187180638_e065f7f1-2373-4db7-ab57-6d40d699d35b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/us/00election-security1/merlin_187180638_e065f7f1-2373-4db7-ab57-6d40d699d35b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/us/00election-security1/merlin_187180638_e065f7f1-2373-4db7-ab57-6d40d699d35b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/us/00election-security1/00election-security1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/08/20/us/00election-security1/00election-security1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/08/20/us/00election-security1/00election-security1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'G.O.P. Election Reviews Create a New Kind of Security Threat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Machines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dominion Voting Systems Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Fraud (Election Fraud)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conspiracy Theories', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rumors and Misinformation', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-01T09:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a7d94ac-b696-5526-9e2b-c2327934c813', 'word_count': 1722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a7d94ac-b696-5526-9e2b-c2327934c813'}, {'abstract': 'John Akomfrah’s films have shaken up official narratives around Black identity and imperialism. His latest tries to make sense of life in the pandemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/arts/design/john-akomfrah.html', 'snippet': 'John Akomfrah’s films have shaken up official narratives around Black identity and imperialism. His latest tries to make sense of life in the pandemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Shortly before the artist and filmmaker John Akomfrah left Ghana for Britain after a 1966 coup, the nine-year-old-boy had a final encounter with his grandfather, the High Priest of the Akomfrah clan. The venerated old man wore a ring that had passed down through generations, representing the power to bring order to life’s chaos. It seemed like a perfect parting gift for his eldest grandson.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/arts/05akomfrah1/merlin_193320384_5f94ff0e-88b8-4d90-a067-7c05e7b26e38-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/05/arts/05akomfrah1/merlin_193320384_5f94ff0e-88b8-4d90-a067-7c05e7b26e38-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 596}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/arts/05akomfrah1/merlin_193320384_5f94ff0e-88b8-4d90-a067-7c05e7b26e38-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1017, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/arts/05akomfrah1/merlin_193320384_5f94ff0e-88b8-4d90-a067-7c05e7b26e38-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2035, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/arts/05akomfrah1/05akomfrah1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/05/arts/05akomfrah1/05akomfrah1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/arts/05akomfrah1/05akomfrah1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Artist Who Brings Order to Chaos', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Sense of Life’s Chaos', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akomfrah, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Lives Matter Movement', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lisson Gallery (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Personal Profile', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-01T09:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Fullerton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fullerton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25d51547-905f-5f5b-8f9b-e07d99948e14', 'word_count': 1534, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25d51547-905f-5f5b-8f9b-e07d99948e14'}, {'abstract': 'Terry Albury, an idealistic F.B.I. agent, grew so disillusioned by the war on terror that he was willing to leak classified documents — and go to prison for doing it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/magazine/fbi-terrorism-terry-albury.html', 'snippet': 'Terry Albury, an idealistic F.B.I. agent, grew so disillusioned by the war on terror that he was willing to leak classified documents — and go to prison for doing it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early on the morning of Aug. 29, 2017, Terry Albury awoke with a nagging sense of foreboding. It was not yet dawn in Shakopee, Minn., the Minneapolis suburb where Albury, an F.B.I. special agent, lived with his wife and two young children, and he lay in bed for a few minutes, running through the mental checklist of cases and meetings and phone calls, the things that generally made him feel as if his life was in order. He was a 16-year veteran of the F.B.I.: 38, tall and powerfully built, with buzzed black hair and a black goatee. Most of his career he had spent in counterterrorism, investigating sleeper cells and racking up commendations signed by the F.B.I. directors Robert Mueller and James Comey, which praised his “outstanding” work recruiting confidential sources and exposing terrorist financing networks. He was a careful investigator and a keen observer. “Something is going on behind the scenes that I’m not aware of,” he told his wife the night before. She told him to stop worrying. “You always think there’s something going on.” She was right. But this time he had reason to be apprehensive, even though he’d been careful. The memory card was buried in his closet, tucked into a shirt pocket under a pile of clothes. “Stop being so paranoid,” he told himself. Then he left for work.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-whistleblower-03/05mag-whistleblower-03-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-whistleblower-03/05mag-whistleblower-03-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 740}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-whistleblower-03/05mag-whistleblower-03-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 831, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-whistleblower-03/05mag-whistleblower-03-superJumbo-