N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-01T15:20:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Kelley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kelley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/28b8f341-c784-5944-afde-5a5ec763aed3', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28b8f341-c784-5944-afde-5a5ec763aed3'}, {'abstract': 'An American-born sociologist, she moved to India in the 1970s, helped pioneer the study of castes and drew attention to the lives of the country’s most oppressed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/world/asia/gail-omvedt-dead.html', 'snippet': 'An American-born sociologist, she moved to India in the 1970s, helped pioneer the study of castes and drew attention to the lives of the country’s most oppressed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Omvedt, an anti-caste crusader, scholar and prolific author who championed the cause of India’s marginalized communities and was a leader in the country’s feminist movement, died on Aug. 25 at her home in the western state of Maharashtra. She was 80.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/03/obituaries/30Omvedt2-print2/merlin_193902180_1f7cd160-2dde-4b72-81c2-f793ef1e9a98-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 924, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/03/obituaries/30Omvedt2-print2/merlin_193902180_1f7cd160-2dde-4b72-81c2-f793ef1e9a98-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 924}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/03/obituaries/30Omvedt2-print2/merlin_193902180_1f7cd160-2dde-4b72-81c2-f793ef1e9a98-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 665, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/03/obituaries/30Omvedt2-print2/merlin_193902180_1f7cd160-2dde-4b72-81c2-f793ef1e9a98-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1399, 'width': 908, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/03/obituaries/30Omvedt2-print2/30Omvedt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/03/obituaries/30Omvedt2-print2/30Omvedt2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/03/obituaries/30Omvedt2-print2/30Omvedt2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gail Omvedt, 80, Dies; India Became Her Home, the Caste System Her Cause', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gail Omvedt, 80, Sociologist Dedicated to Studying Castes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Caste Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sociology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of California, Berkeley', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AMBEDKAR, BHIMRAO RAMJI', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Omvedt, Gail (1941-2021)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-01T15:32:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sameer Yasir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sameer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yasir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/a7e93e4c-1941-55e2-ada9-d56fb1805fd2', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a7e93e4c-1941-55e2-ada9-d56fb1805fd2'}, {'abstract': 'In a new exhibition, the artist returns to the subject of his latest movie and explores the connections between two seemingly separate parts of his career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/t-magazine/julian-schnabel-van-gogh.html', 'snippet': 'In a new exhibition, the artist returns to the subject of his latest movie and explores the connections between two seemingly separate parts of his career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Painting and filmmaking are related mediums, but there is a relatively small canon of good films about painters. These are, by my own, probably highly debatable, count: Kenji Mizoguchi’s “Utamaro and His Five Women” (1946), Vincente Minnelli’s “Lust for Life” (1956), John Huston’s “Moulin Rouge” (1952), Andrei Tarkovsky’s “Andrei Rublev” (1969), Peter Greenaway’s “The Draughtsman’s Contract” (1982), Jacque Rivette’s “La Belle Noiseuse” (1990), Ed Harris’s “Pollock” (2000), Julie Taymor’s “Frida” (2002), Mike Leigh’s “Mr. Turner” (2014), Florian Henckel von Donnersmarck’s “Never Look Away” (2018) — and two movies by Julian Schnabel, who is the only director on the list who can also claim to have made a pretty decent living as a painter. His first film, 1996’s “Basquiat,” is about his former contemporary Jean-Michel Basquiat, and is part biopic (the title character is played by the great Jeffrey Wright), part artistic treatise and almost as much about Schnabel, who actually painted the imitations of Basquiat works that appear in the film himself (he refers to them now as “props”) and shot various scenes inside his own New York City home. His second and superior film about a painter, 2018’s “At Eternity’s Gate,” is an existential portrait of Vincent van Gogh — played by Willem Dafoe — that illustrates the contrast between his pained final days and his outsize influence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/t-magazine/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/01/t-magazine/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/t-magazine/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/t-magazine/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1325, 'width': 1989, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/t-magazine/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/01/t-magazine/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/01/t-magazine/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy/01tmag-schnabel-slide-UIT5-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Julian Schnabel Revisits van Gogh, and Paints Oscar Isaac’s Severed Head', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schnabel, Julian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brant Foundation Art Study Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Gogh, Vincent', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaac, Oscar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-01T15:44:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By M.H. Miller', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd747223-8a09-5244-a350-077a916dc2ee', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd747223-8a09-5244-a350-077a916dc2ee'}, {'abstract': 'A grand jury has issued charges in the 2019 death of Mr. McClain, a young Black man who was put in a chokehold while walking home from a convenience store.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/us/elijah-mcclain-officers-charged-colorado.html', 'snippet': 'A grand jury has issued charges in the 2019 death of Mr. McClain, a young Black man who was put in a chokehold while walking home from a convenience store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — A Colorado grand jury indicted three police officers and two paramedics in the 2019 death of Elijah McClain, a young Black man who had been walking home when he was stopped by the police, put into a chokehold and injected with a powerful anesthetic, the attorney general of Colorado announced on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_p