uri': 'nyt://article/648ae27f-3253-547b-952b-4f5cfcddc5b3'}, {'abstract': 'Radical feminist futures at the Bronx Museum; February James’s excellent New York debut; and sculptures from Argentine Concrete artists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/01/arts/design/art-gallery-shows-reviews.html', 'snippet': 'Radical feminist futures at the Bronx Museum; February James’s excellent New York debut; and sculptures from Argentine Concrete artists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Bronx Museum of the Arts, which turned 50 this year, was founded partly as a way of bringing mainstream art from Manhattan to the borough. Its debut exhibition in 1971 featured loans from the Metropolitan Museum of Art. In the decades since, the programming has been increasingly responsive to global consciousness and its South Bronx neighborhood, making the museum — which is admission free — one of the most adventurous art spaces in the city.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/03/arts/01galleries-3/merlin_193920081_e894440e-1447-45c1-b333-4b8f584effe5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/03/arts/01galleries-3/merlin_193920081_e894440e-1447-45c1-b333-4b8f584effe5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/03/arts/01galleries-3/merlin_193920081_e894440e-1447-45c1-b333-4b8f584effe5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/03/arts/01galleries-3/merlin_193920081_e894440e-1447-45c1-b333-4b8f584effe5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'su