town Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-02T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/151a633a-77d5-54f1-8724-6aeff0bdfed8', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/151a633a-77d5-54f1-8724-6aeff0bdfed8'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes the poem sings when you say it, and then sings more when you say it again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/02/magazine/poem-flight.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes the poem sings when you say it, and then sings more when you say it again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sometimes the poem sings when you say it, and then sings more when you say it again. Take these lines: “Forget the years that only grow harder/as the soul recedes in what the years bring.” I hear it and say, “Yes, I’ve been there.” And you feel a bit of sorrow at how you’ve changed. You wonder why the poem has taken you to such sadness. But the singing keeps going, and you’re now like Lenny Williams, crying, “Oh, I love you, baby,” into some night. And saying: “Touch me. As I am. As you can./My heart a bird’s heart just beyond your hand.” Selected by Reginald Dwayne Betts', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-poem/05mag-poem-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-poem/05mag-poem-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-poem/05mag-poem-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-poem/05mag-poem-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-poem/05mag-poem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-poem/05mag-poem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-poem/05mag-poem-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: Flight', 'kicker': 'Poem', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiman, Christian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-02T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christian Wiman and Reginald Dwayne Betts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wiman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Reginald', 'middlename': 'Dwayne', 'lastname': 'Betts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c514e6b-1769-5e