nt': 1413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/623c492d-695f-54ad-b7d4-c24b0fa07711'}, {'abstract': 'The release of “Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings” is a meaningful moment for Asian American representation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/02/opinion/asian-americans-superheroes-shang-chi.html', 'snippet': 'The release of “Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings” is a meaningful moment for Asian American representation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I and many of my Asian American peers were growing up, we were so hungry to see ourselves represented that we’d scream and call the family to join us in the living room when an Asian guest star wandered into a scene on TV or a commercial came on featuring an Asian family. We’d scour celebrities’ biographies to surface “undercover Asians,” those with trace evidence of Asian heritage. Phoebe Cates, yes! Joseph Gordon-Levitt, no.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/01Yang2/01Yang2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/01Yang2/01Yang2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/01Yang2/01Yang2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/01Yang2/01Yang2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/01Yang2/01Yang2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/01Yang2/01Yang2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/01Yang2/01Yang2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Asian Americans Are Finally Getting the Heroes We Deserve', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Kind of Superheroes We Deserve', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asian-Americans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-02T09:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Yang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a656aaef-64c6-5eb3-84df-5722bf75c2f3', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a656aaef-64c6-5eb3-84df-5722bf75c2f3'}, {'abstract': 'In her new essay collection, the writer wants to enunciate all the meanings and manifestations of the word that our current conversation obscures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/02/magazine/maggie-nelson-on-freedom.html', 'snippet': 'In her new essay collection, the writer wants to enunciate all the meanings and manifestations of the word that our current conversation obscures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was June when I arrived in Northeast Los Angeles, right in the middle of Pride Month, though there wasn’t much evidence of it. In the Bay Area, where I arrived from, rainbow flags, storefront decorations and clumsy attempts at inclusive marketing were ubiquitous. But here, in Southern California’s stupefying sunlight, there were, thankfully, no billboards equating the freedom to date whom you want to the freedom to order weed via an app. Driving along Colorado Boulevard, I encountered only the confusing jumble of gentrification: mom-and-pop doughnut shops next to high-concept pet day cares. In the light, the entire city seemed to be shrugging at me.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-Nelson/05mag-Nelson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-Nelson/05mag-Nelson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 733}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-Nelson/05mag-Nelson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-Nelson/05mag-Nelson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1676, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-Nelson/05mag-Nelson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/05/magazine/05mag-Nelson/05mag-Nelson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtyp