ld', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Cahalan, Andrea Kannapell and Alison Saldanha', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cahalan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andrea', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kannapell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saldanha', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33902e2f-e8cb-50d5-b9a4-9a0f8ee37fa8', 'word_count': 318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33902e2f-e8cb-50d5-b9a4-9a0f8ee37fa8'}, {'abstract': 'A series of changes, big and small, has a strengthened Everton believing it can hold its own with deep-pocketed rivals in England’s Women’s Super League.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/03/sports/soccer/womens-super-league-everton-manchester-city.html', 'snippet': 'A series of changes, big and small, has a strengthened Everton believing it can hold its own with deep-pocketed rivals in England’s Women’s Super League.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIVERPOOL, England — Some of the changes have been small, so small as to be imperceptible, at least from the outside. This summer, for the first time, Everton hired someone specifically to take care of the uniforms of its women’s team. It is the sort of thing that serves as a reminder that, in women’s soccer, many little battles are still being won.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/sports/03soccer-evertonwomen1-print/merlin_194134995_86950f0d-a5fe-42e0-a9f2-ecb0abf5b018-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/04