a Webster and Raillan Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jolie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ruben', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Raillan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d63d395a-bf51-5c8f-907a-6048abb3bd9b', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d63d395a-bf51-5c8f-907a-6048abb3bd9b'}, {'abstract': 'After the disruptions of 2020, teams from coast to coast are playing in their own stadiums for the first time since 2019.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/03/sports/ncaafootball/college-football-home-games-new-mexico.html', 'snippet': 'After the disruptions of 2020, teams from coast to coast are playing in their own stadiums for the first time since 2019.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ALBUQUERQUE — Normalcy, or what passes for it these days, started for Louis Trujillo when he arrived around 6 a.m. on Thursday to tailgate at the University of New Mexico. Ordinary came for Yolanda Sanchez when she began her shift in a stadium parking lot at 7 a.m., and for Andrew Erickson, a Lobos wide receiver, as he warmed up in sight of the Sandia Mountains about 10 hours later.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/sports/03cfb-newmexico1-print/merlin_194114883_a5082e81-7015-462f-853f-c584e014bb7d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/04/sports/03cfb-newmexico1-print/merlin_194114883_a5082e81-7015-462f-853f-c584e014bb7d-articleLarg