ontext.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/04/opinion/biden-job-approval-rating.html', 'snippet': 'Putting presidential approval in context.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Biden’s job approval rating is on the downslope. As of Friday morning he was at 45.8 percent approval and 48.5 percent disapproval — from a high of 54 percent approval, 41 percent disapproval at the end of his first 100 days.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/04bouie-newsletter-lead/merlin_156754548_3c4c2055-e19b-45da-8558-de63a31d678d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/04bouie-newsletter-lead/merlin_156754548_3c4c2055-e19b-45da-8558-de63a31d678d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/04bouie-newsletter-lead/merlin_156754548_3c4c2055-e19b-45da-8558-de63a31d678d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/04bouie-newsletter-lead/merlin_156754548_3c4c2055-e19b-45da-8558-de63a31d678d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/04bouie-newsletter-lead/merlin_156754548_3c4c2055-e19b-45da-8558-de63a31d678d-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/04bouie-newsletter-lead/merlin_156754548_3c4c2055-e19b-45da-8558-de63a31d678d-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/04/opinion/04bouie-newsletter-lead/merlin_156754548_3c4c2055-e19b-45da-8558-de63a31d678d-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Has Joe Biden Become So Unpopular?', 'kicker': 'Jamelle Bouie', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'internal-sub-only', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-04T15:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamelle Bouie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bouie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/baa39b3a-55ad-569f-840a-08b736ac5eaa', 'word_count': 1720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baa39b3a-55ad-569f-840a-08b736ac5eaa'}, {'abstract': 'The Texas abortion law is just an early salvo in a broader push by conservatives to restrict the rights of their neighbors, classmates and colleagues.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/04/opinion/texas-abortion-law.html', 'snippet': 'The Texas abortion law is just an early salvo in a broader push by conservatives to restrict the rights of their neighbors, classmates and colleagues.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the seemingly endless battle to deny disfavored groups equal citizenship, Republican lawmakers around the country have repurposed an old tool to new and cruel effect. They’ve inverted private enforcement laws — marshaled over the years to discipline fraudulent government contractors, racist or sexist bosses and toxic polluters — to enable individuals to suppress the rights of their neighbors, classmates and colleagues. Most prominent among these new laws is SB 8, Texas’s heartbeat bill. The law bans abortions six weeks into a pregnancy, lets anyone bring a lawsuit against medical practitioners who violate the ban and provides cash bounties of at least $10,000 (plus legal fees and costs) to encourage such litigation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/06/opinion/04michaelsnoll1/merlin_179706753_0916f6c0-b010-4cd3-9e29-95b5c4f4c5a0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/06/opinion/04michaelsnoll1/merlin_179706753_0916f6c0-b010-4cd3-9e29-95b5c4f4c5a0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/06/opinion/04michaelsnoll1/merlin_179706753_0916f6c0-b010-4cd3-9e29-95b5c4f4c5a0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/06/opinion/04michaelsnoll1/merlin_179706753_0916f6c0-b010-4cd3-9e29-95b5c4f4c5a0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/06/opinion/04michaelsnoll1/04michaelsnoll1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/06/opinion/04michaelsnoll1/04michaelsnoll1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLar