bscure but chillingly prescient book-length poem from the twilight of the Jazz Age, tell us about our own era?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/06/t-magazine/wild-party-roaring-twenties.html', 'snippet': 'What does “The Wild Party,” an obscure but chillingly prescient book-length poem from the twilight of the Jazz Age, tell us about our own era?', 'lead_paragraph': 'THERE ARE FEW things more glamorous than the belief that we are living through the end of an era — and there are even fewer times in recent history when we haven’t believed it. It’s a conviction that allows us to ennoble ourselves with pathos, with rueful maturity, with wisdom won too late. To be certain that we’re at the beginning of something can mean feeling optimistic and openhearted about the future in a way that, especially these days, risks courting contempt. And to know that we’re in the middle of an era is — well, it’s not even a phrase, is it? It’s nothing much at all, simply a kind of semipermanent Wednesday of the soul, a spirit-flattening acceptance of stasis and complacency. But nearing the end? In that, you have a lifetime’s worth of wistfulness, and perhaps some bitterness and grief, not to mention prescience about what might come next. In short, life at the end of an era is — to use a term that might be coming to the end of its own era — lit. And it almost doesn’t matter if the lighting is seductive and flattering or as harsh and glaring as if the music has just been turned off and the club is about to close. Drama is drama.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '93', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/06/t-magazine/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy/06tmag-wildparty-slide-ENWF-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cautionary Tale for the New Roaring Twenties', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Time of Our Lives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Twenties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Wild Party (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'March, Joseph Moncure', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, 