rent as “King Richard,” about Venus and Serena Williams’s father, and “Petite Maman,” filmmakers can’t stop thinking about children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/06/movies/telluride-film-festival.html', 'snippet': 'In movies as different as “King Richard,” about Venus and Serena Williams’s father, and “Petite Maman,” filmmakers can’t stop thinking about children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TELLURIDE, Colo. — Masks were mandatory in the screening rooms, as well as in the shuttle vans and gondola cars that ferry cinephiles around this gilded former mining town over the Labor Day weekend. If you had a badge, it meant you also had a vaccination and a negative Covid test. Attending the Telluride Film Festival has always meant waiting in a lot of lines, and there was a new queue this year, outside a tent at the edge of a park where you could get your nostrils swabbed.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/arts/06telluride-notebook1/merlin_184615020_f4383c84-75c9-461e-9d4d-39194db36128-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/07/arts/06telluride-notebook1/merlin_184615020_f4383c84-75c9-461e-9d4d-39194db36128-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/arts/06telluride-notebook1/merlin_184615020_f4383c84-75c9-461e-9d4d-39194db36128-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 553, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/arts/06telluride-notebook1/merlin_184615020_f4383c84-75c9-461e-9d4d-39194db36128-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1107, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/arts/06telluride-notebook1/06telluride-notebook1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/07/arts/06telluride-notebook1/06telluride-notebook1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/arts/06telluride-notebook1/06telluride-notebook1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Telluride Film Festival, Both Magic and Normalcy', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At Telluride, ScenesOf Surreal Normality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telluride Film Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Cow (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Spencer (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The French Dispatch (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'King Richard (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Petite Maman (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-06T18:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a2f8d3c-3a7b-5b5f-a427-ffe71599409f', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a2f8d3c-3a7b-5b5f-a427-ffe71599409f'}, {'abstract': 'The company’s decision to reverse course on a proposed ban of “sexually explicit” content shows the power of pornography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/06/opinion/onlyfans-sex-work-safety.html', 'snippet': 'The company’s decision to reverse course on a proposed ban of “sexually explicit” content shows the power of pornography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We are living in the world pornography has made. For more than three decades, researchers have documented that it desensitizes consumers to violence and spreads rape myths and other lies about women’s sexuality. In doing so, it normalizes itself, becoming ever more pervasive, intrusive and dangerous, surrounding us ever more intimately, grooming the culture so that it becomes hard even to recognize its harms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/sunday/03mackinnon/03mackinnon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/sunday/03mackinnon/03mackinnon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/sunday/03mackinnon/03mackinnon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/sunday/03mackinnon/03mackinnon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/sunday/03mackinnon/03mackinnon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/sunday/03mackinnon/03mackinnon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/sunday/03mackinnon/03mackinnon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'OnlyFans Is Not a Safe Platform for ‘Sex Work.’ It’s a Pimp.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'OnlyFans Is Not a Safe Place for ‘Sex Work’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prostitution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pornography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-06T19:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catharine A. MacKinnon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catharine', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'MacKinnon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/25c382be-0d86-5620-889b-f487db888995', 'word_count': 1372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25c382be-0d86-5620-889b-f487db888995'}, {'abstract': 'There is no legitimate religious basis for exemptions from vaccine mandates in any established stream of Christianity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/06/opinion/religious-exemptions-vaccine-mandates.html', 'snippet': 'There is no legitimate religious basis for exemptions from vaccine mandates in any established stream of Christianity.', 'lead_paragraph': '