snippet': 'On his new album, the Nicaraguan Canadian producer considers the political expressions embedded in moments of stillness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brandon Valdivia’s “Momento Presente” is like a summons. On the arresting track from his September album, “Máscaras,” an offbeat, not-quite-footwork rhythm thumps under the swirls of a tin whistle. A bell chimes, and before long, the godlike voice of an elder intones a call to action. “Right now, the oppressors and the oppressed are being separated,” it reflects in Spanish. “We’re not going to wait 2,000 years for the good ones to be on one side and the bad ones to be on another. We are living in that moment now.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '90', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-mas-aya2/merlin_193613640_15b63bae-2dee-4055-9cf8-c4e9d7228acc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-mas-aya2/merlin_193613640_15b63bae-2dee-4055-9cf8-c4e9d7228acc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-mas-aya2/merlin_193613640_15b63bae-2dee-4055-9cf8-c4e9d7228acc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-mas-aya2/merlin_193613640_15b63bae-2dee-4055-9cf8-c4e9d7228acc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-mas-aya2/19new-mas-aya2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, '