subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/books/review/beautiful-country/beautiful-country-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1348, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/books/review/beautiful-country/beautiful-country-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/07/books/review/beautiful-country/beautiful-country-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/books/review/beautiful-country/beautiful-country-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Beautiful Country,’ by Qian Julie Wang: An Excerpt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-09-07T11:45:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fb2f74f-14a4-5067-b4c3-5ebd2c7eaf41', 'word_count': 3052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fb2f74f-14a4-5067-b4c3-5ebd2c7eaf41'}, {'abstract': 'With the help of a Casablancan designer, one expat art dealer creates a home that’s always undergoing its next update.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/07/t-magazine/tangier-morocco-home-design.html', 'snippet': 'With the help of a Casablancan designer, one expat art dealer creates a home that’s always undergoing its next update.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN THE COLLECTIVE Western imagination, Morocco is arid and desertlike, the clay-walled labyrinths of Marrakesh’s medina standing in for the entire country. But Tangier, 350 miles to the city’s north, at the edge of the Rif Mountains where the Atlantic meets the Mediterranean, is humid: Torrential rains fall from New Year’s to Easter, and then sporadically the rest of the year. Wallpaper bubbles, paint flakes and shoes left in the back of the closet turn green with mold. In summer, plumes of fog hover over the Casbah, the city’s historic walled fortress.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/t-magazine/07tmag-gonzalezaller-slide-KNVT/07tmag-gonzalesaller-slide-KNVT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/07/t-magazine/07tmag-gonzalezaller-slide-KNVT/07tmag-gonzalesaller-slide-KNVT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/t-magazine/07tmag-gonzalezaller-slide-KNVT/07tmag-gonzalesaller-slide-KNVT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/t-magazine/07tmag-gonzalezaller-slide-KNVT/07tmag-gonzalesaller-slide-KNVT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1433, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/t-magazine/07tmag-gonzalezaller-slide-KNVT/07tmag-gonzalesaller-slide-KNVT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/07/t-magazine/07tmag-gonzalezaller-slide-KNVT/07t