ole': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tankersley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a49a7d4-39cc-51a7-9da5-6e0e43962114', 'word_count': 1714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a49a7d4-39cc-51a7-9da5-6e0e43962114'}, {'abstract': 'Katherine Lewin opened Big Night, a bright store stocked with everything you need for entertaining.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/07/dining/big-night-store-dinner-party.html', 'snippet': 'Katherine Lewin opened Big Night, a bright store stocked with everything you need for entertaining.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a year of the pandemic, Katherine Lewin, the former editorial director for the restaurant platform the Infatuation, missed dinner parties. Figuring she was not alone, Ms. Lewin opened a bright shop stocked with essentials for entertaining. “People are intimidated, but it can be easy,” she said. (Ms. Lewin readily dispenses advice.) Shelves are filled with food products like tinned seafood, crackers and condiments, and there is a refrigerator stocked with cured meats and cheeses. She also sells She Wolf breads. The central counter and the wall behind it hold flatware, dishes, cake stands, linen napkins, barware and glassware, including some vintage pieces. Behind the store there is a secluded outdoor area with benches and a big picnic table; she plans to hold events with local restaurants there. E-commerce is coming.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-party/06Burner-party-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-party/06Burner-party-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-party/06Burner-party-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-party/06Burner-party-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-party/06Burner-party-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-party/06Burner-party-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-party/06Burner-party-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shop for All Your Dinner Party Needs', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Entertain: Dinner Party Items All in One Place', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Big Night (Manhattan, NY, Retailer)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-07T20:57:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3407729d-fe4e-5b67-be3a-ed676bb676f6', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3407729d-fe4e-5b67-be3a-ed676bb676f6'}, {'abstract': 'The West Village chocolates and salts store closed a year ago, and will reopen on Mulberry Street.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/07/dining/the-meadow-manhattan.html', 'snippet': 'The West Village chocolates and salts store closed a year ago, and will reopen on Mulberry Street.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A year ago, Mark Bitterman closed the Meadow, his West Village shop with its unusual inventory of chocolate bars, salts and bitters. After closing down during the pandemic, he has now relocated across town. At the deep, narrow store furnished with reclaimed lumber you can buy a different chocolate bar for almost every day of the year — he has a wall of more than 350 of them. And you could easily get lost exploring the more than 100 salts from various sources, many flavored, on the shelves opposite. Other products include fresh flowers, salt blocks for cooking and grilling, and a few grocery items like condiments and spices. Among the newer chocolates he’s carrying, almost all bean-to-bar, are Honeymoon from St. Louis, Bixby from Maine and Cuna de Piedra from Monterrey, Mexico. You might also get to know the elegant Sol Cacao bars from the Bronx. Among the salts are a saffron variety, a useful seasoning that’s difficult to produce, and a very popular Guatemalan fleur de sel and ground Tellicherry pepper mix, which isn’t.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-Shop/merlin_194138523_c55ce0d7-b488-42b1-9ad8-a8eecba47c0a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-Shop/merlin_194138523_c55ce0d7-b488-42b1-9ad8-a8eecba47c0a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-Shop/merlin_194138523_c55ce0d7-b488-42b1-9ad8-a8eecba47c0a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-Shop/merlin_194138523_c55ce0d7-b488-42b1-9ad8-a8eecba47c0a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-Shop/merlin_194138523_c55ce0d7-b488-42b1-9ad8-a8eecba47c0a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-Shop/merlin_194138523_c55ce0d7-b488-42b1-9ad8-a8eecba47c0a-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/dining/06Burner-Shop/merlin_194138523_c55ce0d7-b488-42b1-9ad8-a8eecba47c0a-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Meadow Moves Across Town', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Shop: The Meadow Moves  Across Manhattan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Meadow, The (Bitterman & Sons Inc)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value