ge-or-deaths.html', 'snippet': 'Emergency services in Guerrero said there were reports of power loss and issues with phone service across the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Andrés Manuel López Obrador, in a video shared on Twitter at about 11 p.m. Eastern time, said there was no significant damage in the state of Guerrero, the quake’s epicenter, or in the neighboring states of Morelos, Oaxaca, Puebla or the capital, Mexico City, after a 7.1 magnitude earthquake hit the Mexican resort town of Acapulco on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/07/world/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials/merlin_194356032_e5e04886-c7dd-4f83-8d97-84b76dfa171c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/10/07/world/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials/merlin_194356032_e5e04886-c7dd-4f83-8d97-84b76dfa171c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/07/world/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials/merlin_194356032_e5e04886-c7dd-4f83-8d97-84b76dfa171c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/07/world/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials/merlin_194356032_e5e04886-c7dd-4f83-8d97-84b76dfa171c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/07/world/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/10/07/world/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/07/world/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials/07mexico-earthquake-briefing-officials-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico’s president said there are no immediate reports of serious damage or deaths.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-09-08T03:22:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jesus Jiménez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jesus', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jiménez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/703296a3-9ba2-5881-93ab-27cac502d7c5', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/703296a3-9ba2-5881-93ab-27cac502d7c5'}, {'abstract': 'Captain America and Spider-Man remember those lost on Sept. 11 in an eight-page story that is included in some Marvel comics out Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/08/arts/marvel-new-comic-9-11.html', 'snippet': 'Captain America and Spider-Man remember those lost on Sept. 11 in an eight-page story that is included in some Marvel comics out Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, “The Four Fives,” an eight-page story from Marvel Entertainment in remembrance of the lives lost on Sept. 11, will publish. In the nearly dialogue-free comic, Spider-Man and Captain America are in downtown Manhattan as the Bell of Hope, in the churchyard of St. Paul’s Chapel, rings in a pattern of “four fives” (five strikes, four times): a longstanding ritual that signals a firefighter has fallen. The comic was written by Joe Quesada; drawn by John Romita Jr. and Scott Hanna; colored by \u200b\u200bMarte Gracia; and lettered by Joe Caramagna.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/08comic-911_image2/08comic-911_image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 464, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/08comic-911_image2/08comic-911_image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 464}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/08comic-911_image2/08comic-911_image2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/08comic-911_image2/08comic-911_image2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/08comic-911_image2/08comic-911_image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/08comic-911_image2/08comic-911_image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/08comic-911_image2/08comic-911_image2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marvel’s Heroes Reflect on 9/11 in New Story', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marvel Heroes Reflect on 9/11 in a New Story', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spider-Man (Fictional Character)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marvel Entertainment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quesada, Joe', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romita, John Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-08T04:01:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de509488-d9ae-530e-9dbb-2a63870abb6b', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de509488-d9ae-530e-9dbb-2a63870abb6b'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t remember the name? Vinci was one of the greatest spoilers in tennis history, ending Serena Williams’s Grand Slam hopes in 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/08/sports/tennis/us-open-serena-williams-roberta-vinci.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t remember the name? Vinci was one of the greatest spoilers in tennis history, ending Serena Williams’s Grand Slam hopes in 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2015, Roberta Vinci improbably put an end to Serena Williams’s bid for a Grand Slam at the U.S. Open and called it “the best moment of my life.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/sports/07usopen-spoilers-web-1/merlin_990485