pe': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/us/08extreme-weather-briefing-nursing-homes/08extreme-weather-briefing-nursing-homes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/08/us/08extreme-weather-briefing-nursing-homes/08extreme-weather-briefing-nursing-homes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/us/08extreme-weather-briefing-nursing-homes/08extreme-weather-briefing-nursing-homes-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seven Louisiana nursing homes lose their licenses after evacuating residents to a warehouse.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-09-08T09:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felice Belman and Sophie Kasakove', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sophie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kasakove', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1f978e6-d222-522c-b7db-bfd14ae4357d', 'word_count': 387, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1f978e6-d222-522c-b7db-bfd14ae4357d'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer Rachel Bujalski traveled to the Oregon towns burned by the Almeda fire last year even before she had an assignment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/08/insider/photographs-of-a-housing-crisis-worsened-by-fire.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer Rachel Bujalski traveled to the Oregon towns burned by the Almeda fire last year even before she had an assignment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the past decade, Rachel Bujalski, a photographer based in San Francisco, has been documenting the inability of many people to find affordable housing in the United States. As part of this work, she has examined the devastating impact of wildfires that have left thousands of people homeless. She recently traveled to Ashland, Ore., in a region where the Almeda fire destroyed thousands of homes last September, and recorded the experiences of residents who are still displaced a year later for an article that was published Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/pageoneplus/08a2_itt-6/merlin_192105174_048ef79b-6a0f-4d81-9560-bc750f3292eb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/08/pageoneplus/08a2_itt-6/merlin_192105174_048ef79b-6a0f-4d81-9560-bc750f3292eb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/pageoneplus/08a2_itt-6/merlin_192105174_048ef79b-6a0f-4d81-9560-bc750f3292eb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/pageoneplus/08a2_itt-6/merlin_192105174_048ef79b-6a0f-4d81-9560-bc750f3292eb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2