_works', 'value': 'Morning Sun (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stephens, Simon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Blair', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Falco, Edie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ireland, Marin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Manhattan Theater Club', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-08T09:02:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Soloski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soloski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b3d3af1-f79f-560e-90f0-3ee805fa24f8', 'word_count': 1571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b3d3af1-f79f-560e-90f0-3ee805fa24f8'}, {'abstract': 'With the growing visibility of gender-nonconforming and transgender people, the scope of feminism is fast evolving. Now two major museum shows in California explore the impact on art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/08/arts/design/feminist-transgender-nonbinary-art.html', 'snippet': 'With the growing visibility of gender-nonconforming and transgender people, the scope of feminism is fast evolving. Now two major museum shows in California explore the impact on art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Organizing a museum survey of feminist art can be as politically fraught as organizing a women’s march, for some of the same reasons. Different women are bound to have different political goals or priorities. There are competing theoretical frameworks, from Marxist feminism, which sees capitalism as the main source of women’s oppression, to the intersectional feminism so prominent today, which highlights the impact of factors such as race and class on women’s lives. And the very notion of what it means to be a woman is fast evolving, with the growing visibility of gender-fluid, nonbinary and transgender populations.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '98', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo/19NEW-FEMINIST-ART-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Gender Alchemy’ Is Transforming Art for the 21st Century', 'kicker': 'Fall Preview', 'content_k