cohol was more hindrance than help. The question had been popularized by the sober-curious movement, based on a term coined by the British author Ruby Warrington, and supported by online recovery programs such as Tempest, founded in 2014. But it became especially acute as the incoherent national response to the Covid-19 pandemic conspired with a failing health care system to prove once again that the state could not be trusted to ensure its citizens’ wellness. This was particularly true, the reanimated Black Lives Matter movement announced, when those citizens were brown or Black.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '48', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/t-magazine/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/09/t-magazine/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/t-magazine/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/t-magazine/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 1333, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/t-magazine/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy/09tmag-blackrecovery-slide-SI2K-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width