s and Trade Shows', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-09T17:09:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Will Heinrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heinrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3e24505-95f7-5cfa-a4a0-4682f45bd43c', 'word_count': 1561, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3e24505-95f7-5cfa-a4a0-4682f45bd43c'}, {'abstract': 'Oscar Isaac, Tiffany Haddish and Willem Dafoe star in the latest head trip from Paul Schrader, a story about betting on life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/09/movies/the-card-counter-review.html', 'snippet': 'Oscar Isaac, Tiffany Haddish and Willem Dafoe star in the latest head trip from Paul Schrader, a story about betting on life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man sits writing in a room, alone in his head, alone in the world. We hear his words, his thoughts, in a voice-over that’s a portal to his reality. It’s an intimate, unmodulated voice, and what he says is often unremarkable to the point of banality. Yet something troubles the man which, in turn, troubles you. He may be a good man gone wrong or a bad one gone right; the only thing certain is that he jumped out of the head of Paul Schrader.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/00card-counter/merlin_194009259_c99df4d3-2a38-4e7c-b128-b444fe7c34c8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/00card-counter/merlin_194009259_c99df4d3-2a38-4e7c-b128-b444fe7c34c8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/00card-counter/merlin_194009259_c99df4d3-2a38-4e7c-b128-b444fe7c34c8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/00card-counter/merlin_194009259_c99df4d3-2a38-4e7c-b128-b444fe7c34c8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1231, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/00card-counter/00card-counter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/00card-counter/00card-counter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/00card-counter/00card-counter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Card Counter’ Review: A Gambler’s Existential Solitaire', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Out of Prison, He Finds A New One', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Card Counter (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schrader, Paul', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Isaac, Oscar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-09T17:09:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cb776f0-4702-5a62-9b68-9b6a5148749f', 'word_count': 1198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cb776f0-4702-5a62-9b68-9b6a5148749f'}, {'abstract': 'This documentary underscores the hard-fought lessons the immunologist learned during the AIDS pandemic. Many shape his resolve now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/09/movies/fauci-review.html', 'snippet': 'This documentary underscores the hard-fought lessons the immunologist learned during the AIDS pandemic. Many shape his resolve now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In their sympathetic portrait “Fauci,” John Hoffman and Janet Tobias introduce Dr. Anthony S. Fauci, the director of the National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, with a split-screen. On one side, the man who has been the face of the nation’s Covid-19 response leaves his home with a security detail. Next to this gray-haired public health figure unspools news footage of a younger Dr. Fauci walking up stairs to begin, as a reporter states, “his 12-hour day.” At the time, he was leading the nation’s H.I.V./AIDS response.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/fauci1/fauci1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/fauci1/fauci1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/fauci1/fauci1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/fauci1/fauci1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/fauci1/fauci1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/fauci1/fauci1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/08/arts/fauci1/fauci1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Fauci’ Review: The First Pandemic That Shaped the Good Doc', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fauci', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fauci (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fauci, Anthony S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoffman, John (Screenwriter)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tobias, Janet', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-09T17:17:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbbb9e78-e7f8-5326-917e-b4ff5425567e', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbbb9e78-e7f8-5326-917e-b4ff5425567e'}, {'abstract': 'For the defending New Jersey field-hockey state champions, last year was a season of frustration and loss — and this year’s tryouts are a chance to rebuild', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/09/magazine/field-hockey-new-jersey.html', 'snippet': 'For the defending New Jersey field-hockey state champions, last year was a season of frustration and loss — and this year’s tryouts are a chance to rebuild', 'lead_paragraph': 'If the guiding spirits of high school sports are competition, fellowship and common purpose, the 2020-21 school year brought challenges to them all. Close-knit teams, accustomed to the physical camaraderie of the locker room or the huddle, had to keep their distance socially; coaches, used to the normal pattern of practices and games, found themselves canceling sessions, posting workouts online and doing their best to send encouraging emails to their players. In some cases, entire seasons were called off.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/magazine/12mag-fieldhockey-FPO-25-copy/12mag-fieldhockey-FPO-25-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/12/magazine/12mag-fieldhockey-FPO-25-copy/12mag-fieldhockey-FPO-25-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/magazine/12mag-fieldhockey-FPO-25-copy/12mag-fieldhockey-FPO-25-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i