paragraph': 'At the bottom of the Pacific Ocean, cylindrical clusters of the glass sponge Euplectella aspergillum jut upward like skyscrapers in the deep sea. Some house tiny shrimp, to whom an 11-inch sponge is essentially a high-rise. And the sponge’s glass skeleton is certainly a feat of architecture, comprising a geometric latticework that gives the sponge the illusion of being wrapped in lace. Yet it is enduringly sturdy, able to stay rooted in the sea floor and weather currents without snapping or splintering.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/science/09tb-sponge-1/09tb-sponge-1--articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/21/science/09tb-sponge-1/09tb-sponge-1--articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/science/09tb-sponge-1/09tb-sponge-1--jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/science/09tb-sponge-1/09tb-sponge-1--superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/science/09tb-sponge-1/09tb-sponge-1--thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/21/science/09tb-sponge-1/09tb-sponge-1--thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/science/09tb-sponge-1/09tb-sponge-1--thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Swirling Vortex Is No Match for This Deep-Sea Sponge', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tough and Tender: Why This Delicate Sea Sponge Is So Hard to Wipe Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skeletons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Glass', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of the Royal Society Interface', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Ocean', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-09T17:44:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sabrina Imbler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sabrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Imbler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ce1cb62-adcf-54cc-bb22-45e3e88cae5e', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ce1cb62-adcf-54cc-bb22-45e3e88cae5e'}, {'abstract': 'More companies are requiring employees to be vaccinated, but their approaches vary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/09/business/corporate-vaccine-mandates.html', 'snippet': 'More companies are requiring employees to be vaccinated, but their approaches vary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The issue of vaccine mandates has been a delicate balance for employers, weaving in politics, health and privacy. But the government has put increasing pressure on employers to pla