}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Hazards and Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chevron Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citigroup Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delta Air Lines Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Goldman Sachs Group Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Airlines', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-09T17:52:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lauren Hirsch and Coral Murphy Marcos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lauren', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirsch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Coral', 'middlename': 'Murphy', 'lastname': 'Marcos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ee7eeae-de7e-537d-ae9c-26367a87de20', 'word_count': 1034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ee7eeae-de7e-537d-ae9c-26367a87de20'}, {'abstract': 'The chief executive of the airline’s parent company said he hoped the policy would be in place “by Christmas."', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/09/travel/qantas-vaccine-mandate-international.html', 'snippet': 'The chief executive of the airline’s parent company said he hoped the policy would be in place “by Christmas."', 'lead_paragraph': 'Qantas, Australia’s largest airline, will require that all passengers on international flights are vaccinated against the coronavirus when it restarts worldwide operations in December, its chief executive said Wednesday, making it one of the first airlines in the world to require proof of vaccination for everyone on board.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/arts/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/09/arts/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/arts/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/arts/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/arts/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/09/arts/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/arts/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1/09virus-briefing-qantas-vaccine-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Qantas becomes one of the first airlines to require that international passengers be vaccinated.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Qantas Airways', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-09T17:59:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Heather Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Heather', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b908747c-8cfe-550d-9582-dfaf1838a9f8', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b908747c-8cfe-550d-9582-dfaf1838a9f8'}, {'abstract': 'Let your fall re-entry begin at the Independent Art Fair in Manhattan, which features painting, photography and the pioneers of net art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/09/arts/design/independent-art-fair-cipriani.html', 'snippet': 'Let your fall re-entry begin at the Independent Art Fair in Manhattan, which features painting, photography and the pioneers of net art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Coming up in the ’90s, “independent” (often shortened to “indie”) signaled culture that was maverick, authentic and relatively low budget. It meant movies that weren’t Hollywood-blockbuster types and music not released on corporate record labels. And while art didn’t necessarily follow the same ethos, or economic model, the Independent Art Fair, founded by fellow Gen-Xers Elizabeth Dee and Matthew Higgs, kind of felt like it did.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09independent-review1/merlin_194417709_1a03fb8b-e9e4-4f16-8875-600093c37b12-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09independent-review1/merlin_194417709_1a03fb8b-e9e4-4f16-8875-600093c37b12-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09independent-review1/merlin_194417709_1a03fb8b-e9e4-4f16-8875-600093c37b12-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09independent-review1/merlin_194417709_1a03fb8b-e9e4-4f16-8875-600093c37b12-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09independent-review1/merlin_194417709_1a03fb8b-e9e4-4f16-8875-600093c37b12-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09independent-review1/merlin_194417709_1a03fb8b-e9e4-4f16-8875-600093c37b12-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {