s amassed almost 100 titles, including the 1973 volume “Slimming Down,” written by Johnny Carson’s sidekick, Ed McMahon. “Slimming Down” — which featured chapter titles like “The Breadstick Conspiracy” and “Two Martinis Into Connecticut” — is the book that began Ms. Gordon’s collection.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/02maintenance1/merlin_193990476_8b741d57-4ade-4940-81d9-0b40a142b72b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/02maintenance1/merlin_193990476_8b741d57-4ade-4940-81d9-0b40a142b72b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/02maintenance1/merlin_193990476_8b741d57-4ade-4940-81d9-0b40a142b72b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/02maintenance1/merlin_193990476_8b741d57-4ade-4940-81d9-0b40a142b72b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/02maintenance1/merlin_193990476_8b741d57-4ade-4940-81d9-0b40a142b72b-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/02maintenance1/merlin_193990476_8b741d57-4ade-4940-81d9-0b40a142b72b-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/02maintenance1/merlin_193990476_8b741d57-4ade-4940-81d9-0b40a142b72b-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Breaking Down the ‘Wellness-Industrial Complex,’ an Episode at a Time', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Analyzing the ‘Wellness-Industrial Complex’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Maintenance Phase (Radio Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Aubrey (Podcast Host)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hobbes, Michael', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-09T19:11:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victoria Petersen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Petersen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b4e5849-d9da-5108-8326-671417860783', 'word_count': 1321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b4e5849-d9da-5108-8326-671417860783'}, {'abstract': 'The Colombian star skips innovation and presents an impressionistic inventory of the sounds that established him as a global force on his sixth studio album.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/09/arts/music/j-balvin-jose-review.html', 'snippet': 'The Colombian star skips innovation and presents an impressionistic inventory of the sounds that established him as a global force on his sixth studio album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If there is one figure in pop music who has perfected the language of feel-good cultural affirmation, it is J Balvin. For over a decade, the 36-year-old Colombian star has claimed he is on a mission to “change the perception of Latinos in music,” using his rainbow aesthetics, smooth reggaeton textures and radio-ready trap hits as ammunition.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09BALVIN-REVIEW1/merlin_194065326_5efb20fa-3bfc-4b2f-979d-55c79aaebafe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09BALVIN-REVIEW1/merlin_194065326_5efb20fa-3bfc-4b2f-979d-55c79aaebafe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09BALVIN-REVIEW1/merlin_194065326_5efb20fa-3bfc-4b2f-979d-55c79aaebafe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09BALVIN-REVIEW1/merlin_194065326_5efb20fa-3bfc-4b2f-979d-55c79aaebafe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09BALVIN-REVIEW1/09BALVIN-REVIEW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09BALVIN-REVIEW1/09BALVIN-REVIEW1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/arts/09BALVIN-REVIEW1/09BALVIN-REVIEW1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'J Balvin Attempts to Reintroduce Himself on ‘Jose’', 'kicker': 'Album Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Let J Balvin Reintroduce Himself', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'J Balvin (1985- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Jose (Album)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Latin Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-09T19:21:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Isabelia Herrera', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Isabelia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Herrera', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/66d37979-b564-5dab-903b-9be3b8b95335', 'word_count': 736, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66d37979-b564-5dab-903b-9be3b8b95335'}, {'abstract': 'The relationship between the use of standardized tests in college admissions and diversity on campus is far from clear. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/09/opinion/sat-standardized-tests-ucs.html', 'snippet': 'The relationship between the use of standardized tests in college admissions and diversity on campus is far from clear. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'In May of this year, the University of California Board of Regents, which makes decisions for a system that educates 280,000 students across 10 campuses, announced it would end the use of the SAT and ACT in the U.C. admissions process, effective immediately. This was a departure from a year before, when the regents, who had suspended the use of the test for Covid pandemic reasons, revealed a plan to phase out the tests over the next five years. But then a lawsuit got settled that forced the U.C. system to speed up the timeline and make the change permanent, with vague plans to begin using a customized test by 2025. (Those plans have been put on hold.) The initial, slower timeline should not be seen as a sign of reticence on the board’s part, however; when it voted in 2020 on whether to phase out the tests, the vote was 23-0.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/09kang/09kang-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/09kang/09kang-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/09kang/09kang-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/09kang/09kang-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1080, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/09kang/09kang-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/09kang/09kang-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/opinion/09kang/09kang-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': 