ation of an instrument to help him preen his feathers appears to be unique, researchers say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/10/science/kea-beak-tools.html', 'snippet': 'The bird is a kea from New Zealand, and his fabrication of an instrument to help him preen his feathers appears to be unique, researchers say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many animals are known to use tools, but a bird named Bruce may be one of the most ingenious nonhuman tool inventors of all: He is a disabled parrot who has designed and uses his own prosthetic beak.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bruce Is a Parrot With a Broken Beak. So He Invented a Tool.', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brilliant Bird: A Parrot With a Broken Beak Comes Up With a Good Imitation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parrots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Cognition', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Behavior', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Scientific Reports (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Zealand', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-animals', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-10T09:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0aa791d-4b81-5f5c-8a40-5990ca425056', 'word_count': 567, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0aa791d-4b81-5f5c-8a40-5990ca425056'}, {'abstract': 'After “Game of Thrones,” many said the blockbuster series was dead. Maybe not — but the future of TV epics may look more like the movies’ recent past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/10/arts/television/future-tv-blockbuster-shows.html', 'snippet': 'After “Game of Thrones,” many said the blockbuster series was dead. Maybe not — but the future of TV epics may look more like the movies’ recent past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In spring 2019, as “Game of Thrones” aired its final season, the talk among TV-industry pundits was that the age of dragons was not the only era coming to an end. “Thrones,” the thinking went, might just be the last big TV series ever: That is, the last blockbuster-level behemoth that would dazzle and focus the obsession of a mass audience.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '74', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-season-critic-illo-SUB/19new-season-critic-illo-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-season-critic-illo-SUB/19new-season-critic-illo-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-season-critic-illo-SUB/19new-season-critic-illo-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-season-critic-illo-SUB/19new-season-critic-illo-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'ran