}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/52718ec4-84cb-54dd-bcce-5edf7be71aac', 'word_count': 353, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52718ec4-84cb-54dd-bcce-5edf7be71aac'}, {'abstract': 'The 2021 U.S. Open has by no means been conventional, but amid a fluctuating pandemic, it has been a notable milestone on the road to tennis and civic normality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/10/sports/us-open-attendance.html', 'snippet': 'The 2021 U.S. Open has by no means been conventional, but amid a fluctuating pandemic, it has been a notable milestone on the road to tennis and civic normality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It began with a human traffic jam and could end with a Grand Slam. There were unprecedented and initially confusing medical requirements and a massive storm that stranded spectators and flooded courts. Some of the game’s biggest stars did not play, but a host of intriguing new ones took advantage of their absence and electrified audiences that seemed to make more noise than ever.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/11/sports/10usopen-assessment1-print/merlin_194359197_d9d090b6-1539-404d-ad24-5c42b475b94c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/11/sports/10usopen-assessment1-print/merlin_194359197_d9d090b6-1539-404d-ad24-5c42b475b94c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/11/sports/10usopen-assessment1-print/merlin_194359197_d9d090b6-1539-404d-ad24-5c42b475b94c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/11/sport