major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raducanu, Emma (2002- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fernandez, Leylah (2002- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-10T11:46:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Clarey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ade1a6dd-504c-55ac-9067-e9f9972080a3', 'word_count': 1553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ade1a6dd-504c-55ac-9067-e9f9972080a3'}, {'abstract': 'As disease and death reigned around them, some Americans declared that they would never get vaccinated and raged at government efforts to compel them. Anti-vaccination groups spread propaganda about terrible side effects and corrupt doctors. State officials tried to ban mandates, and people made fake vaccination certificates to evade inoculation rules already in place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/10/world/vaccination-mandates-are-an-american-tradition-and-so-is-the-backlash.html', 'snippet': '', 'lead_paragraph': 'As disease and death reigned around them, some Americans declared that they would never get vaccinated and raged at government efforts to compel them. Anti-vaccination groups spread propaganda about terrible side effects and corrupt doctors. State officials tried to ban mandates, and people made fake vaccination certificates to evade inoculation rules already in place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/09/us/politics/09-politicsbrief-vaxhistory/09onpolitics-pm-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height