: 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smell (Olfaction)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quarantine (Life and Culture)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-10T15:56:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce7a5511-e5f1-52d5-8750-1885ff10521a', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce7a5511-e5f1-52d5-8750-1885ff10521a'}, {'abstract': 'These sticks, cones, coils and papers can help you clear your head, define a space and even rediscover a sense of time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/10/t-magazine/incense-guide.html', 'snippet': 'These sticks, cones, coils and papers can help you clear your head, define a space and even rediscover a sense of time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American acid-rock band the Strawberry Alarm Clock’s 1967 song “Incense and Peppermints” inevitably recalls the pervasiveness of scents like patchouli during the hippie era. “Occasions, persuasions clutter your mind / Incense and peppermints, the color of time,” the lead singer croons. But lyrics like these — co-written by John S. Carter and Tim Gilbert — also nod, if only accidentally, to the widespread use of incense in our own helter-skelter age.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/10/t-magazine/10tmag-incense-extra-slide-GPE3-copy/10tmag-incense-extra-slide-GPE3-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/10/t-magazine/10tmag-incense-extra