o analysis and interviews at the site cast doubt on that account.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — It was the last known missile fired by the United States in its 20-year war in Afghanistan, and the military called it a “righteous strike” — a drone attack after hours of surveillance on Aug. 29 against a vehicle that American officials thought contained an ISIS bomb and posed an imminent threat to troops at Kabul’s airport.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Investigation: In U.S. Drone Strike, Evidence Suggests No ISIS Bomb', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Evidence Disputes U.S. Claim of ISIS Bomb in Kabul Drone Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kabul (Afghanistan)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State Khorasan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-10T20:09:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthieu Aikins, Christoph Koettl, Evan Hill and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthieu', 'middlename': None, 'last