o-soldiers-get-statue-at-west-point.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Saturday, September 11, 2021', 'lead_paragraph': '“When I was coming up we had no role models that we could talk to. We didn’t know we had Buffalo Soldiers. If we had known about that it would have made a difference. Now they have a historical, tangible reference point.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day: Buffalo Soldiers Get Statue at West Point', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quote of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-09-11T03:46:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9911cd1-df63-5715-9823-49e2664e9ffb', 'word_count': 76, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9911cd1-df63-5715-9823-49e2664e9ffb'}, {'abstract': 'Howard Garfinkel co-founded the Five Star Basketball Camp, which trained big-name stars like Michael Jordan, Patrick Ewing and Grant Hill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/11/sports/basketball/howard-garfinkel-five-star-basketball-camp.html', 'snippet': 'Howard Garfinkel co-founded the Five Star Basketball Camp, which trained big-name stars like Michael Jordan, Patrick Ewing and Grant Hill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grant Hill was introduced to the Five Star Basketball Camp in the form of a Sports Illustrated article that was published in 1984, when he was 11 years old. As Hill flipped through the pages of the magazine, he found himself transfixed. To him, Five Star sounded like basketball nirvana, an exclusive destination where promising players could consume the game.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image