he wealthy and ignored those who suffered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/11/opinion/purdue-sacklers-opioids-oxycontin-settlement.html', 'snippet': 'The Purdue Pharma bankruptcy case settlement protected the wealthy and ignored those who suffered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sept. 26, 2019, the Department of Justice appointed me to serve on the Official Unsecured Creditors Committee in the bankruptcy case against Purdue Pharma, the company that helped fuel the opioid overdose crisis through the misbranding and reckless marketing of the powerful painkiller OxyContin. The committee acted as a mega-plaintiff, with broad powers to subpoena records, take depositions and cross-examine witnesses. For nearly two years, I attended countless negotiations, depositions and chambers meetings. I read thousands of pages of confidential documents revealing the true nature and depth of Purdue’s liability in the crisis.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/sunday/10Hampton/10Hampton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/sunday/10Hampton/10Hampton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/sunday/10Hampton/10Hampton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/sunday/10Hampton/10Hampton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1800, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/sunday/10Hampton/10Hampton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/sunday/10Hampton/10Hampton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/sunday/10Hampton/10Hampton-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sacklers Are Walking Off Into the Sunset. Reform the System.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Betraying the Victims of the Opioid Crisis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Purdue Pharma', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sackler Family', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opioids and Opiates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'OxyContin (Drug)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Compensation for Damages (Law)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pain-Relieving Drugs', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-11T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ryan Hampton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hampton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad86ba0e-c571-535e-96ab-3a11464b9e07', 'word_count': 1288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad86ba0e-c571-535e-96ab-3a11464b9e07'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty years after the worst attack on American soil, the loss of nearly 3,000 people was remembered in events across the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/11/nyregion/9-11-anniversary-ceremonies.html', 'snippet': 'Twenty years after the worst attack on American soil, the loss of nearly 3,000 people was remembered in events across the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The loved ones gathered again in Lower Manhattan for moments of silence and the peals of the bells. They paid tribute to those they lost 20 years earlier and listened as Bruce Springsteen sang about memory and loss.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/11/multimedia/11sept11-image2/merlin_194527707_a712da9d-23fd-41bc-8b12-e92ab3950aeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/11/multimedia/11sept11-image2/merlin_194527707_a712da9d-23fd-41bc-8b12-e92ab3950aeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/11/multimedia/11sept11-image2/merlin_194527707_a712da9d-23fd-41bc-8b12-e92ab3950aeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/11/multimedia/11sept11-image2/merlin_194527707_a712da9d-23fd-41bc-8b12-e92ab3950aeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima