//www.nytimes.com/2021/09/12/world/europe/pope-francis-viktor-orban-hungary.html', 'snippet': 'On a quick trip to the country, Francis met with Prime Minister Viktor Orban, Hungary’s hard-right leader, before celebrating a public Mass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BUDAPEST — Pope Francis used his short time in Budapest on Sunday to urge his bishops to embrace diversity and send a message to the country’s hard-right, anti-migrant leader, Prime Minister Viktor Orban, that God is not a strongman who silences enemies and that religious roots, while vital for a country, also allow it to open up and extend “its arms toward everyone.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/world/12pope1/merlin_194593323_74a6faba-8625-4d22-b8ed-7fd44b1cb7fa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/12/world/12pope1/merlin_194593323_74a6faba-8625-4d22-b8ed-7fd44b1cb7fa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/world/12pope1/merlin_194593323_74a6faba-8625-4d22-b8ed-7fd44b1cb7fa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/world/12pope1/merlin_194593323_74a6faba-8625-4d22-b8ed-7fd44b1cb7fa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/world/12pope1/12pope1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/12/world/12pope1/12pope1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/world/12pope1/12pope1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Orban’s Hungary, Pope Urges Bishops to Embrace Diversity', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In an Increasingly Isolated Hungary, Francis Urges Diversity', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orban, Viktor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Budapest (Hungary)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-12T13:32:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Horowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09061e40-6179-587e-980e-0a8586c3868c', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09061e40-6179-587e-980e-0a8586c3868c'}, {'abstract': 'As Omar Little, the actor bent his beautiful mind to a task that even the best writers and showrunners often avoid. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/12/opinion/michael-k-williams-david-simon-the-wire.html', 'snippet': 'As Omar Little, the actor bent his beautiful mind to a task that even the best writers and showrunners often avoid. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'The second season of our fledgling HBO drama in Baltimore did not shoot its first frame of film before one key cast member was in the writers’ offices, scripts in hand, showing his disappointment.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/12Simon-04/12Simon-04-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/12Simon-04/12Simon-04-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/12Simon-04/12Simon-04-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/12Simon-04/12Simon-04-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/12Simon-04/12Simon-04-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/12Simon-04/12Simon-04-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/12Simon-04/12Simon-04-thumbLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Question Michael K. Williams Asked Me Before Every Season of ‘The Wire’', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Selfless Art of Michael K. Williams', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Michael Kenneth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Wire (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Actors and Actresses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simon, David (1960- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-12T13:57:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Simon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f9da303-4b54-5143-8fce-4fd5d64fe681', 'word_count': 1422, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f9da303-4b54-5143-8fce-4fd5d64fe681'}, {'abstract': "History shows us that what counts as a threat to a womans life isn't always clear-cut.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/12/opinion/abortion-texas-roe.html', 'snippet': "History shows us that what counts as a threat to a womans life isn't always clear-cut.", 'lead_paragraph': 'Join us, if you will, in a thought experiment. It’s the fall of 2022. Dr. H., an obstetrician-gynecologist, practices in a red state. Much has changed in the reproductive rights landscape by then: In the spring, her state rushed to pass a law similar to the notorious 2021 Texas law that bans a large majority of abortions and incentivizes private citizens to sue anyone helping someone get an abortion. The Supreme Court also overturned Roe v. Wade in the Dobbs v. Jackson Women’s Health Organization case that year, leaving the issue of abortion regulation to individual states; a few years before, Dr. H.’s state passed a trigger ban that automatically banned the few abortions that were still legal in the state when Roe fell. In her state, the law now allows an abortion only when a pregnancy threatens the life of a pregnant person.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/12steinauerjoffe/12steinauerjoffe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/12steinauerjoffe/12steinauerjoffe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/12steinauerjoffe/12steinauerjoffe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/12steinauerjoffe/12steinauerjoffe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1482, 'width': 1482, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/12steinauerjoffe/12steinauerjoffe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/12steinauerjoffe/12steinauerjoffe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/opinion/12steinauerjoffe/12steinauerjoffe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}