 dialed an 800 number to ask or complain about something you bought or to make an inquiry about something you’re thinking of buying, there is a decent chance you were profiled — by the arrangement of your words and the tone of your voice — without knowing it. My research suggests many customer contact centers now approach and manage callers based on what they think the person’s voice or syntax reveal about the individual’s emotions, sentiments and personality, often in real time.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/opinion/09turow-01/09turow-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/14/opinion/09turow-01/09turow-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/opinion/09turow-01/09turow-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/opinion/09turow-01/09turow-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/opinion/09turow-01/09turow-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/14/opinion/09turow-01/09turow-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/opinion/09turow-01/09turow-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hear That? It’s Your Voice Being Taken for Profit.', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speakers (Audio)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Automation and Smart Homes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Advertising and Marketing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-12T14:45:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joseph Turow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joseph', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/03224b9a-bfd0-557d-8a5b-e635d02490eb', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03224b9a-bfd0-557d-8a5b-e635d02490eb'}, {'abstract': 'A rabbi’s advice for those who have done wrong and those who can’t forgive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/12/opinion/yom-kippur-forgiveness.html', 'snippet': 'A rabbi’s advice for those who have done wrong and those who can’t forgive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A friend of mine was publicly canceled. He deserved it and he knew it. He spent a year working with a rabbi and a therapist, during which time he tried to track down those he had hurt and apologize to them, often more than once. We can’t see inside one another’s hearts, but I believe in the sincerity of his change.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rabbi’s Guide on Making Amends and Letting Those Grudges Go', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'So You’ve Been Canceled: A Yom Kippur Atonement Guide', 'nam