 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/science/13SCI-BRODY-AGING/13SCI-BRODY-AGING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/14/science/13SCI-BRODY-AGING/13SCI-BRODY-AGING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/science/13SCI-BRODY-AGING/13SCI-BRODY-AGING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/science/13SCI-BRODY-AGING/13SCI-BRODY-AGING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1302, 'width': 1965, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/science/13SCI-BRODY-AGING/13SCI-BRODY-AGING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/14/science/13SCI-BRODY-AGING/13SCI-BRODY-AGING-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/14/science/13SCI-BRODY-AGING/13SCI-BRODY-AGING-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Age Gracefully', 'kicker': 'Personal Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gray Hair Is Fine; Bad Grammar Is (Still) Not', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Falls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Stupid Things I Won't Do When I Get Old (Book)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-13T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Live', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane E. Brody', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Brody', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94f54f7b-44cb-5099-8b59-20200075d05a', 'word_count': 1052, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94f54f7b-44cb-5099-8b59-20200075d05a'}, {'abstract': 'California has not been as progressive lately as its reputation would suggest. Yet Republicans have had trouble breaking the recall out of the fringe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/us/republicans-california-recall-election.html', 'snippet': 'California has not been as progressive lately as its reputation would suggest. Yet Republicans have had trouble breaking the recall out of the fringe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THOUSAND OAKS, Calif. — The small faction of Californians who still call themselves Republicans did something seemingly impossible when they forced Gavin Newsom, the Democratic governor of America’s largest Democratic state, to face voters in a recall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/12/us/politics/12california-gop-1/merlin_194304300_16afab3e-5b79-45d4-b546-956b627946e1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/12/us/politics/12california-gop-1/merlin_194304300_16afab3e-5b79-45d4-b546-956b627946e1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'