nization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06235aba-c14d-5521-987a-3522b69b0447', 'word_count': 1064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06235aba-c14d-5521-987a-3522b69b0447'}, {'abstract': 'The ecosystem in my own yard  is showing signs of both trouble and hope.\xa0', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/opinion/nature-birds-migration.html', 'snippet': 'The ecosystem in my own yard  is showing signs of both trouble and hope.\xa0', 'lead_paragraph': 'NASHVILLE — How ragged we are now, dragging summer behind us like an old blanket we can’t set down. The homicidal heat of August has given way to the merely cruel heat of mid-September, but we are done with it even so. Everyone is cross, and not just the people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13renkl-lead/13renkl-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13renkl-lead/13renkl-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13renkl-lead/13renkl-lead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13renkl-lead/13renkl-lead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13renkl-lead/13renkl-lead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13renkl-lead/13renkl-lead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13renkl-lead/13renkl-lead-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Summer Without Butterflies, I Cling to What Endures', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Migration', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insects', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-13T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Renkl', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Renkl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e1e48e8-bb42-55ae-9f82-5a4f264676f6', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e1e48e8-bb42-55ae-9f82-5a4f264676f6'}, {'abstract': 'Dictionaries reward you for paying attention, both to the things you consume and to your own curiosity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/magazine/dictionary-recommendation.html', 'snippet': 'Dictionaries reward you for paying attention, both to the things you consume and to your own curiosity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I can’t remember how old I was when I first learned the words denotation (the definition of a word) and connotation (the suggestion of a word). But I do remember feeling a little betrayed by the idea that there was a whole layer of language that couldn’t quite be conveyed through a dictionary. Like most young people, I enjoyed learning but thought of it as something I would eventually be done with. At some age, I assumed, I would need to know everything. Understanding the nuances of language seemed like an obstacle to that goal. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-LOR-1/19mag-LOR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-LOR-1/19mag-LOR-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-LOR-1/19mag-LOR-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-LOR-1/19mag-LOR-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1318, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-LOR-1/19mag-LOR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-LOR-1/19mag-LOR-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-LOR-1/19mag-LOR-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Use a Dictionary in the Age of Internet Search?', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dictionaries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dictionaries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merriam-Webster Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-13T09:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel del Valle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Valle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0b2a362-79a6-5797-aea4-c0af586af0aa', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0b2a362-79a6-5797-aea4-c0af586af0aa'}, {'abstract': 'As president, he went on the road to pull the new nation together.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/opinion/politics-infrastructure-george-washington.html', 'snippet': 'As president, he went on the road to pull the new nation together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'These are troubling and rancorous times. Every day there seems to be another headline about the country’s ever-widening political divide. And it’s not just Democrat versus Republican. Within each party the gulf between the extremes is growing as progressives shout angrily at centrists and Donald Trump’s faithful refuse to tolerate the slightest deviation from his ironbound party line. The word “unprecedented” is often used to describe the level of combative partisanship that has gripped the nation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13philbrick-lead/13philbrick-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13philbrick-lead/13philbrick-lead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 737}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13philbrick-lead/13philbrick-lead-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 834, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13philbrick-lead/13philbrick-lead-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1667, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13philbrick-lead/13philbrick-lead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13philbrick-lead/13philbrick-lead-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13philbrick-lead/13philbrick-lead-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'There’s a Very Good Reason ‘Washington Slept Here’', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Revolutionary War, American (1775-83)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Alexander', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jefferson, Thomas', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madison, James (1751-1836)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monroe, James (1758-1831)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, George (1732-99)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-13T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathaniel Philbrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathaniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Philbrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2be48b36-4a0d-5ca6-a122-cca68e3aac30', 'word_count': 1097, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2be48b36-4a0d-5ca6-a122-cca68e3aac30'}, {'abstract': 'The author dissects the anxieties and discontents of living in a world wrought by tech giants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/opinion/sway-kara-swisher-dave-eggers.html', 'snippet': 'The author dissects the anxieties and discontents of living in a world wrought by tech giants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Imagine a world in which Google and Amazon join together to form an all-knowing corporate juggernaut that could program our every movement. Author Dave Eggers has contemplated such a future in his latest dystopian novel “The Every.” Eggers, who limits his own use of technology to the bare minimum, says he was inspired by the limitless choice of our digital world and the idea of a data-driven tech monopoly that would use “your preferences and algorithmic-determined personality” to help you “become the better version of yourself and the ultimate version of yourself.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13sway-eggers-image/13sway-eggers-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13sway-eggers-image/13sway-eggers-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13sway-eggers-image/13sway-eggers-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13sway-eggers-image/13sway-eggers-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13sway-eggers-image/13sway-eggers-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13sway-eggers-image/13sway-eggers-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13sway-eggers-image/13sway-eggers-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dave Eggers Created the Google-Amazon Mash-Up of Your Nightmares', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eggers, Dave', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Commerce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Amazon.com Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bezos, Jeffrey P', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Every (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'audio-neutral-informative', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-13T09:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': "By ‘Sway'", 'person': [{'firstname': "Sway'", 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9ac49ba-8f56-5509-a7a9-48ec7d53eaa2', 'word_count': 265, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9ac49ba-8f56-5509-a7a9-48ec7d53eaa2'}, {'abstract': 'There are many reasons to fear a Chinese invasion of Taiwan. But  the American pullout isn’t one of them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/opinion/china-taiwan-afghanistan.html', 'snippet': 'There are many reasons to fear a Chinese invasion of Taiwan. But  the American pullout isn’t one of them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many reasons to fear an impending Chinese attack on Taiwan: Intensified Chinese aerial activity. High-profile Pentagon warnings. Rapid Chinese military modernization. President Xi Jinping’s escalating rhetoric. But despite what recent feverish discussion in foreign policy and military circles is suggesting, the U.S. withdrawal from Afghanistan isn’t one of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13Mastro-02/merlin_187296951_f32b6c67-573c-4e26-bc97-8fc31ecb4c0f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13Mastro-02/merlin_187296951_f32b6c67-573c-4e26-bc97-8fc31ecb4c0f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13Mastro-02/merlin_187296951_f32b6c67-573c-4e26-bc97-8fc31ecb4c0f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13Mastro-02/merlin_187296951_f32b6c67-573c-4e26-bc97-8fc31ecb4c0f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13Mastro-02/13Mastro-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13Mastro-02/13Mastro-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13Mastro-02/13Mastro-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What the U.S. Withdrawal From Afghanistan Means for Taiwan', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-13T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oriana Skylar Mastro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oriana', 'middlename': 'Skylar', 'lastname': 'Mastro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/11d33e3f-e389-52ca-bdf1-de68a242f61a', 'word_count': 1354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11d33e3f-e389-52ca-bdf1-de68a242f61a'}, {'abstract': 'The newest painting by Jasper Johns was inspired by a fan letter from an astrophysicist. Here’s a first look.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/arts/design/slice-jasper-johns.html', 'snippet': 'The newest painting by Jasper Johns was inspired by a fan letter from an astrophysicist. Here’s a first look.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 91, Jasper Johns is turning out impressive and touchingly personal work. During the solitary months of the pandemic, he completed a painting titled “Slice,” and a group of related drawings and prints. Likely to be a standout of his upcoming show, “Jasper Johns: Mind/Mirror,” a two-venue retrospective opening Sept. 29 at the Whitney Museum of American Art and the Philadelphia Museum of Art, “Slice” is a large, horizontal and predominantly black oil painting that combines unrelated images of a map of outer space and a human knee.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '112', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 461, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 461}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 787, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1574, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1/19new-jasper-johns-sidebar1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'widt