type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Glueck and Dana Rubinstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glueck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Dana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubinstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1973e288-3c3c-5194-83ca-98c02ca2edf0', 'word_count': 1218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1973e288-3c3c-5194-83ca-98c02ca2edf0'}, {'abstract': 'Several key witnesses against Mr. Kelly, who is on trial in Brooklyn, still appear loyal to the singer — but their accounts appear to corroborate the accusations against him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/nyregion/r-kelly-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Several key witnesses against Mr. Kelly, who is on trial in Brooklyn, still appear loyal to the singer — but their accounts appear to corroborate the accusations against him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'R. Kelly and one of his assistants were in a park in Chicago a few years before his 2019 arrest when the singer asked the assistant, Diana Copeland, why she had not acted to prevent one of his girlfriends from packing her suitcase and leaving his home.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/nyregion/13kelly-employees/merlin_193409475_2ffd7cf6-7596-4ed2-99ac-dbd70659e432-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/13/nyregion/13kelly-employees/merlin_193409475_2ffd7cf6-7596-4ed2-99ac-dbd70659e432-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty