t will provoke a response.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On March 19, 1956, The New York Times carried an interview with Matyas Rakosi, who was described as “Hungary’s ebullient Communist boss.” Rakosi said that his enemies had accused him of using “salami tactics,” that is, cutting away all opposition slice by slice. He didn’t deny it: “That is the job of any good political party — including the Communists,” Rakosi said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13coy_new/13coy_new-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13coy_new/13coy_new-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13coy_new/13coy_new-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13coy_new/13coy_new-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13coy_new/13coy_new-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13coy_new/13coy_new-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13coy_new/13coy_new-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Game Theory Says About China’s Strategy', 'kicker': 'peter Coy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'internal-sub-only', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schelling, Thomas C', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salami', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nobel Prizes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hungary', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-13T19:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Coy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8da160d1-10a1-556a-b04c-6df74872c9da', 'word_count': 679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8da160d1-10a1-556a-b04c-6df74872c9da'}, {'abstract': 'The structure of unemployment insurance is broken and does little to help those who pay into it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/opinion/unemployment-reform-covid-biden.html', 'snippet': 'The structure of unemployment insurance is broken and does little to help those who pay into it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The unprecedented federal action to prop up unemployment insurance system during the pandemic wound down last week even as the pace of hiring in the United States slowed dramatically. The wind-down affected nearly 12 million workers — an estimated 5.1 million self-employed, contract and gig workers and 3.8 million long-term unemployed people who lost benefits completely, and three million who kept benefits but lost the $300 weekly federal supplement — bringing the programs created by last March’s CARES Act and renewed by this March’s American Rescue Plan Act to an end.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13edwards/13edwards-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13edwards/13edwards-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13edwards/13edwards-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13edwards/13edwards-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13edwards/13edwards-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13edwards/13edwards-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/13/opinion/13edwards/13edwards-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'America Can Find a Smarter Way to Help Workers Who Have Lost Their Jobs', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub'