w book, “Bewilderment,” came to him when he imagined a child talking to him in a forest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/books/richard-powers-bewilderment.html', 'snippet': 'His Pulitzer-winning novel, “The Overstory,” left him so drained that he didn’t know whether he would write again. His new book, “Bewilderment,” came to him when he imagined a child talking to him in a forest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOWNSEND, Tenn. — On a cool, rainy morning in August, the novelist Richard Powers was in one of his favorite hiding places, a tiny pebble cove along a mountain stream in the Great Smoky Mountains. He has spent countless hours here, writing in his electronic notebook, swimming in the frigid churn until his limbs are numb and staring up at the canopy of alders, sycamore, beech, eastern white pine, hemlock, pawpaw and maple that has become as familiar to him as his own living room.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/books/13RICHARDPOWERS1/merlin_193806813_c590a0a9-bf97-406d-ac28-fac910799f08-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/15/books/13RICHARDPOWERS1/merlin_193806813_c590a0a9-bf97-406d-ac28-fac910799f08-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/books/13RICHARDPOWERS1/merlin_193806813_c590a0a9-bf97-406d-ac28-fac910799f08-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/books/13RICHARDPOWERS1/merlin_193806813_c590a0a9-bf97-406d-ac28-fac910799f08-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJu