wport Jazz Festival', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newport Folk Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newport (RI)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Jazz on a Summer's Day (Movie)", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Festival Productions', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-13T20:31:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Keepnews', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keepnews', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/5eec3c41-eb70-5b6a-aba5-f430c613e457', 'word_count': 2137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5eec3c41-eb70-5b6a-aba5-f430c613e457'}, {'abstract': 'Semblance, made from chardonnay grapes, pairs nicely with food and delivers a zip of carbonation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/dining/drinks/semblance-zero-proof-wine.html', 'snippet': 'Semblance, made from chardonnay grapes, pairs nicely with food and delivers a zip of carbonation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to alcohol-free drinks, a rapidly growing category, the carbonated ones are the most successful. That’s why some of the beers are quite enjoyable. The bubbles often balance the lack of alcohol; without them the products can taste flat. That goes for wine, too. A newcomer, Semblance — a sparkler made with chardonnay grapes harvested from California vineyards in coastal areas — is dry, lightly fruity and pleasant on its own or to savor with a meal. Drinkers won’t miss the alcohol, and it has a winy quality. Traditional winemaking practices, including fermentation in stainless steel tanks, make the base wine. The alcohol is removed using low-temperature vacuum steam distillation, often called spinning cone technology, said to maintain the character of the grapes.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/13Burner-Wine/13Burner-Wine-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/13Burner-Wine/13Burner-Wine-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/13Burner-Wine/13Burner-Wine-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/13Burner-Wine/13Burner-Wine-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1367, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/13Burner-Wine/13Burner-Wine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/13Burner-Wine/13Burner-Wine-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/13Burner-Wine/13Burner-Wine-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Zero-Proof Bubbly for Any Celebration', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sip: Zero-Proof Bubbly For Any Celebration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-13T20:36:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dcc8abd-71b2-5e59-8b95-0c7bcd703cb6', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dcc8abd-71b2-5e59-8b95-0c7bcd703cb6'}, {'abstract': 'The chef Hong Thaimee is serving her pad thai in a new space across the village in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/13/dining/pad-thaimee.html', 'snippet': 'The chef Hong Thaimee is serving her pad thai in a new space across the village in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hong Thaimee, the Thai chef who had the restaurant Ngam in the East Village and pop-ups elsewhere, has now established herself in Greenwich Village with a kitchen for takeaway and deliveries, and a restaurant. Pad Thaimee, selling pad thai, the dish for which she is best known, and a version made with zucchini noodles, was up and running at the end of August. The limited menu also includes a gently-spiced green curry fried rice, and fried rice with Chinese broccoli, egg and anchovies. Chicken, shrimp, soft-shell crab, mixed seafood or tofu can be added to any of the dishes. The easily reheated food comes in boxes lined with banana leaves to hold moisture. A vegan Thai menu, only for takeout and deliveries and called Thaimee Blossom, will be available in November. And Thaimee Love, which was a pop-up at 615 Hudson Street, will also open as a regular restaurant, sharing the same kitchen in several weeks.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/dining/13Burner-Thai/merlin_194486118_e5e57661-a2d9-440d-