rovements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Service', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-14T09:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim McKeough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McKeough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50086d99-6213-518c-8e4b-a68e6cb998b6', 'word_count': 1368, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50086d99-6213-518c-8e4b-a68e6cb998b6'}, {'abstract': 'New galleries for Dutch and Flemish art in Boston, and the arrival of “Afro-Atlantic Histories” in Houston, will complicate serene pictures of the past.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/14/arts/design/historical-museum-exhibits.html', 'snippet': 'New galleries for Dutch and Flemish art in Boston, and the arrival of “Afro-Atlantic Histories” in Houston, will complicate serene pictures of the past.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time during the first year of the pandemic was a continuous present: that was what was worst about it. Days became shapeless, dislodged from the past, divorced from the future; nothing stuck, nothing had endurance; whole months washed over me in a nebulous babble of posts and pics. Rediscovering ourselves means rediscovering time — not the time of push notifications and 14-day infection rates, but a deep, evolutionary time, where who we were informs who we are and who we will be.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '104', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtyp