ion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John McWhorter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McWhorter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/32cbd086-fda6-5ee0-bc3e-57472f3f2f65', 'word_count': 1450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32cbd086-fda6-5ee0-bc3e-57472f3f2f65'}, {'abstract': 'From October to December, we’re hosting four free webinars to help teachers use our mentor texts, vocabulary features, and narrative and profile-writing contests in their classrooms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/14/learning/fall-webinar-series-teaching-with-the-new-york-times.html', 'snippet': 'From October to December, we’re hosting four free webinars to help teachers use our mentor texts, vocabulary features, and narrative and profile-writing contests in their classrooms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Teachers have told us how much they value participating in our live events with a community of educators — even if the events take place virtually — because they connect teachers from around the world with each other and The Times. And that’s our goal with our fall webinar series: In four free professional development sessions from October to December, we will explore using The New York Times to teach and learn with personal narratives, mentor texts, vocabulary and journalistic profiles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/02/learning/FallWebTopArtLN/FallWebTopArtLN-articleLarge.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/02/learning/FallWebTopArtLN/FallWebTopArtLN-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/02/learning/FallWebTo