 on the solution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARVADA, Colo. — President Biden warned on Tuesday that the United States had only a decade left to confront a global climate crisis, using his second day touring a wildfire-ravaged West to try to rally the public, and congressional Democrats, to support measures that his administration hopes will reduce the burning of fossil fuels.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Urges Climate Action: ‘We Don’t Have Much More Than 10 Years’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Urging Action On Climate,  Biden Warns Time Is Short', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Jobs Plan (2021)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Renewable Energy Laboratory', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Arvada (Colo)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boise (Idaho)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-14T23:07:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zolan Kanno-Youngs and Jim Tankersley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zolan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kanno-Youngs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tankersley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e793a1d-25f6-58e0-8142-818ed919e6ba', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://articl