le': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/497948cd-fa64-5402-b958-3d218c7c4c70', 'word_count': 1477, 'uri': 'nyt://article/497948cd-fa64-5402-b958-3d218c7c4c70'}, {'abstract': 'During the brief moment when the pandemic was receding and we could be together again, all we wanted to do was move our bodies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/15/magazine/dancing-new-york-summer.html', 'snippet': 'During the brief moment when the pandemic was receding and we could be together again, all we wanted to do was move our bodies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For most of 2020, I passed the pandemic alone in my studio apartment. I turned 33, then 34, and my body seemed to grow old without bringing my spirit along with it. My right knee was clearly deteriorating — I couldn’t sit cross-legged at my desk the way I used to — and because I wasn’t wearing makeup, I could track each age spot as it bloomed to the surface. When I pulled my hair back in a tight ponytail, I could see a patch of scalp. But in that same period had my life evolved at all? Had I met anyone? Surprised myself? Stemmed the tide of collective crisis? My mother often urged me to dance, just a little, by myself in the kitchen — “It’s good medicine,” she said, “despojo.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-Dancing-images/19mag-Dancing-images-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-Dancing-images/19mag-Dancing-images-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-Dancing-images/19mag-Dancing-images-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-Dancing-images/19mag-Dancing-images-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1639, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-Dancing-images/19mag-Dancing-images-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-Dancing-images/19mag-Dancing-images-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/magazine/19mag-Dancing-images/19mag-Dancing-images-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dancing Through New York in a Summer of Joy and Grief', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bodies on the Line ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salsa Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus Reopenings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Summer (Season)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-15T09:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carina del Valle Schorske', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Valle', 'q