or, apologized for “inexcusable” failures in the investigation of Lawrence G. Nassar, who sexually abused hundreds of women and girls.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/15/sports/olympics/fbi-hearing-larry-nassar-biles-maroney.html', 'snippet': 'Christopher A. Wray, the F.B.I. director, apologized for “inexcusable” failures in the investigation of Lawrence G. Nassar, who sexually abused hundreds of women and girls.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Sitting at a witness table alongside three of her former gymnastics teammates, Simone Biles broke down in tears while explaining to a Senate committee that she doesn’t want any more young people to experience the kind of suffering she endured at the hands of Lawrence G. Nassar, the former national team doctor.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Biles and Her Teammates Rip the F.B.I. for Botching Nassar Abuse Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gymnasts Tell of Betrayal That Followed Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gymnastics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nassar, Lawrence G (1963- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biles, Simone', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maroney, McKayla', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raisman, Aly', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Gymnastics', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wray, Christopher A', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-15T13:38:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Macur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14c11f2d-482c-50bc-ae03-d2cc2dbf1e4e', 'word_count': 1607, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14c11f2d-482c-50bc-ae03-d2cc2dbf1e4e'}, {'abstract': 'He may have been best known for his work on “Saturday Night Live,” but he should be really remembered for decades of club sets and you-can’t-miss-this clips.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/15/arts/television/norm-macdonald-comedy.html', 'snippet': 'He may have been best known for his work on “Saturday Night Live,” but he should be really remembered for decades of club sets and you-can’t-miss-this clips.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My favorite Norm Macdonald joke — and trust me, there’s serious competition — is one he told as anchor of Weekend Update on “Saturday Night Live” in the late 1990s. Papers in front of him, he reported with a cheer: “Yippie! Jerry Rubin died this week.” Looking down, he apologized for his mistake and tried again: “That should read: ‘Yippie Jerry Rubin died this week.’”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/16/arts/14macdonald-appraisal/14macdonald-appraisal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge':