k of whale hunters who follow a centuries-old tradition that helps feed local people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/15/world/europe/dolphins-killed-faroe-islands.html', 'snippet': 'Graphic images of the animals raised ire among activists, and some locals said the killings undermined the work of whale hunters who follow a centuries-old tradition that helps feed local people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The custom of whale and dolphin hunting, known as grindadrap, is a centuries-old practice in the Faroe Islands and a key part of many locals’ diet. And many Faroese point to regulations — including rules around the killing of mammals — aimed at making the practice sustainable as a reason to keep the tradition alive.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/world/15dolphins01/merlin_194742255_d3013a49-7bbc-4673-9d5a-7bd549bb6cb6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/15/world/15dolphins01/merlin_194742255_d3013a49-7bbc-4673-9d5a-7bd549bb6cb6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/world/15dolphins01/merlin_194742255_d3013a49-7bbc-4673-9d5a-7bd549bb6cb6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/world/15dolphins01/merlin_194742255_d3013a49-7bbc-4673-9d5a-7bd549bb6cb6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/world/15dolphins01/15dolphins