som-governor-california.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Gavin Newsom is facing multiple crises. Ninety percent of California is in extreme drought. The median home price has eclipsed $800,000. Some 100,000 people are sleeping outside or in their cars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SACRAMENTO — For nearly a year — while a pandemic raged, while wildfires roared, while smoke smothered the once-pristine blue skies over Lake Tahoe — Gov. Gavin Newsom has had to simultaneously govern the nation’s most populous state and beat back an attempted recall.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Newsom Beat the Recall, Now Comes the Hard Part: Governing California', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Rebuffing Recall,  Newsom Pivots to Face  Many California Crises', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Newsom, Gavin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, California Gubernatorial Recall (2021)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-15T22:21:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shawn Hubler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shawn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hubler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e91a2488-538f-51bc-aea1-a465405ef452', 'word_count': 1157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e91a2488-538f-51bc-aea1-a465405ef452'}, {'abstract': 'On Pier 76 in Hudson River Park, the brand staged a youthful, wide-ranging show complete with skateboarders and drummers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/15/t-magazine/coach-new-york-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'On Pier 76 in Hudson River Park, the brand staged a youthful, wide-ranging show complete with skateboarders and drummers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Thursday afternoon, Stuart Vevers switched on his laptop camera to accept an Accessories Council Hall of Fame Award for the Rogue, a boxy leather handbag he debuted in 2016, a couple years into his tenure as creative director of Coach. “In the last year and half, I’ve been thinking about the role Coach has played in people’s lives, over so many decades,” Vevers said to a virtual audience from the office on the top floor of his Upper West Side townhouse, one shoeless foot tucked beneath him, out of the frame. “It stands for beautifully made pieces that capture the optimistic spirit of New York, our forever muse.” The moment encapsulated a purposeful set of contrasts — quality craftsmanship and laid-back dress, reverence for the past and forward-looking zeal — scheduled to go on grander display the following evening at Coach’s spring 2022 runway presentation at Hudson River Park’s Pier 76, which promised to mark a triumphant if open-aired return to live viewing.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/t-magazine/fashion/Coach-48hours-slide-ADC2/Coach-48hours-slide-ADC2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/15/t-magazine/fashion/Coach-48hours-slide-ADC2/Coach-48hours-slide-ADC2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/15/t-magazine/fashion/Coach-48hours-slide-ADC2/Coach-48hours-slide-ADC2