ead-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/17/reader-center/17Cancel_lead/17Cancel_lead-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'I Will Never Forget That I Could Have Lived With People Who Loved Me', 'kicker': 'Guest Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Foster Care System Is Broken', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foster Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Adoptions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Group Homes and Supportive Housing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-16T09:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sixto Cancel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sixto', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cancel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae6d0ea4-bcee-5e73-b43e-11427acd5ce7', 'word_count': 1405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae6d0ea4-bcee-5e73-b43e-11427acd5ce7'}, {'abstract': 'Brace yourself for an onslaught of devices that connect your eyes to the digital world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/16/opinion/face-computers-virtual-reality.html', 'snippet': 'Brace yourself for an onslaught of devices that connect your eyes to the digital world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is difficult to avoid sounding vulgar, somehow, when discussing the future of facial computing. There is somethin