’s efforts to combat it (“The Dope,” by Benjamin T. Smith), along with an argument that modern warfare is too easy (Samuel Moyn’s “Humane”) and a memoir by a key figure in Donald Trump’s first impeachment (Alexander Vindman’s “Here, Right Matters”). We’ve got a hardscrabble immigration memoir from Qian Julie Wang, “Beautiful Country,” and two books exploring aspects of technology: Meghan O’Gieblyn’s “God, Human, Animal, Machine” and Tom Standage’s “A Brief History of Motion.” And in fiction, we recommend three debut novels about characters trying to make the best of sometimes dire circumstances: “Paris Is a Party, Paris Is a Ghost,” by David Hoon Kim, “Three Rooms,” by Jo Hamya, and “The Love Songs of W.E.B. Du Bois,” by the accomplished poet Honorée Fanonne Jeffers.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/16/books/16RecBooks/16RecBooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/16/books/16RecBooks/16RecBooks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/16/books/16RecBooks/16RecBooks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 511, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/16/books/16RecBooks/16RecBooks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1364, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/16/books/16RecBooks/16RecBooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/16/books/16RecBooks/16RecBooks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/16/books/16RecBooks/16RecBooks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '9 New Books We Recommend This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Staff Picks From the Book Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamya, Jo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeffers, Honoree Fanonne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim, David Hoon (Author)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moyn, Samuel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Gieblyn, Meghan", 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Standage, Tom', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vindman, Alexander S', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wang, Qian Julie', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Benjamin T (Scholar)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Brief History of Motion: From the Wheel, to the Car, to What Comes Next (Book)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Beautiful Country: A Memoir (Book)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'God, Human, Animal, Machine: Technology, Metaphor, and the Search for Meaning (Book)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Here, Right Matters: An American Story (Book)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Humane: How the United States Abandoned Peace and Reinvented War (Book)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'cr