rts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elysa Gardner, Jeremy Gordon, Olivia Horn, Jon Pareles, Giovanni Russonello and Lindsay Zoladz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elysa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Olivia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Horn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Giovanni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Russonello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}, {'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zoladz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 6}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/596a0017-349e-5109-b98c-5ca732c363fc', 'word_count': 6814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/596a0017-349e-5109-b98c-5ca732c363fc'}, {'abstract': 'Timely plays tackle tough subjects, while musicals get the royal treatment, thanks to a princess (“Diana”), queens (“Six”) and the King of Pop (“MJ”).', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/17/theater/broadway-theater-plays-musicals.html', 'snippet': 'Timely plays tackle tough subjects, while musicals get the royal treatment, thanks to a princess (“Diana”), queens (“Six”) and the King of Pop (“MJ”).', 'lead_paragraph': 'In another season, the chance to see “Wicked” or “The Lion King” again after so long wouldn’t be such thrilling news. But this isn’t any other theater season. So while in these listings we detail plenty of world premieres (“Flying Over Sunset,” “The Bedwetter”); inventive revivals (a gender-swapped “Company”); and at least seven plays by Black writers on Broadway, we might also take a look at the old reliables. Welcome back.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-THEATER-LISTINGS-nov1/merlin_170122809_dc4725da-bc04-4a27-958b-cff06dc55dfb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 443, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-THEATER-LISTINGS-nov1/merlin_170122809_dc4725da-bc04-4a27-958b-cff06dc55dfb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 443}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-THEATER-LISTINGS-nov1/merlin_170122809_dc4725da-bc04-4a27-958b-cff06dc55dfb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 756, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-THEATER-LISTINGS-nov1/merlin_170122809_dc4725da-bc04-4a27-958b-cff06dc55dfb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1512, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-THEATER-LISTINGS-nov1/merlin_170122809_dc4725da-bc04-4a27-958b-cff06dc55dfb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-THEATER-LISTINGS-nov1/merlin_170122809_dc4725da-bc04-4a27-958b-cff06dc55dfb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/19/arts/19NEW-THEATER-LI