/17/world/europe/imperial-measurements-pounds-ounces-return.html', 'snippet': 'The government announced plans to allow shops to sell produce in pounds and ounces, rather than using the metric system, as part of an effort to “capitalize on new Brexit freedoms.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British government said it was taking steps to return to its traditional system of imperial weights and measures, allowing shops and market stalls to sell fruits and vegetables labeled in pounds and ounces alone, rather than in the metric system’s grams and kilograms, a move it hailed as an example of the country’s new post-Brexit freedoms.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/18/multimedia/17xp-imperial-units1-print/merlin_180554499_eb56024a-ec4e-49a6-ab9c-79bd2efab05a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/18/multimedia/17xp-imperial-units1-print/merlin_180554499_eb56024a-ec4e-49a6-ab9c-79bd2efab05a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/18/multimedia/17xp-imperial-units1-print/merlin_180554499_eb56024a-ec4e-49a6-ab9c-79bd2efab05a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/18/multimedia/17xp-imperial-units1-print/merlin_180554499_eb56024a-ec4e-49a6-ab9c-79bd2efab05a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/18/multimedia/17xp-imperial-units1-print/merlin_180