'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Abortion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-18T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Letters', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/c85fc99f-f47b-58a0-8d3a-27e22eb8802e', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c85fc99f-f47b-58a0-8d3a-27e22eb8802e'}, {'abstract': 'Competition for market share at rock-bottom prices has led to\xa0shortages, price spikes, allegations of price-fixing and substandard and even dangerous practices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/18/opinion/drug-market-prescription-generic.html', 'snippet': 'Competition for market share at rock-bottom prices has led to\xa0shortages, price spikes, allegations of price-fixing and substandard and even dangerous practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American health care system is built on the idea that a pill is a pill. Generic drugs are considered equal to and interchangeable with one another — and also with the name brand. This gospel has existed since 1984, when a law known as Hatch-Waxman was passed, allowing companies to make drugs that had gone off patent without having to replicate the same expensive clinical trials. For the most part, all they had to do was prove that the generic was manufactured using good practices and worked in the body in a similar way, within an acceptable range.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/18/opinion/18stockman_square/18stockman_square-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/18/opinion/18stockman_square/18stockman_square-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/18/opinion/18stockman_square/18stockman_square-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/18/opinion/18stockman_square/18stockman_square-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/18/opinion/18stockman_square/18stockman_square-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/18/opinion/18stockman_square/18stockman_square-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/18/opinion/18stockman_square/18stockman_square-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Drug Supply Is Sick. How Can We Fix It?', 'kicker': 'Farah Stockman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Drug Supply  Is Sick. How Can  We Fix It?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub