at looks simple but develops into satisfying complexity. I went to the archives to see if it was new, and found that The New York Times has run three of them before, all by Matt Ginsburg, between 2009 and 2015. Alex Eaton-Salners constructed today’s grid; variety connoisseurs may be reminded of another of his specialties, the “Going Too Far” puzzles. Easy directions lead to a creative workout and a challenging solve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Variety: Takeaway Crossword', 'kicker': 'Sunday VARIETY COLUMN', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eaton-Salners, Alex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-18T16:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caitlin Lovinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caitlin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lovinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/192fa40b-3126-5440-bc16-16b4589cfc6e', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/192fa40b-3126-5440-bc16-16b4589cfc6e'}, {'abstract': 'Gambling on football has come out of the shadows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/18/opinion/NFL-gambling-bets.html', 'snippet': 'Gambling on football has come out of the shadows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you watched the N.F.L.’s first weekend of action, there is a good chance you saw more ads for BetMGM, FanDuel and Caesars Sportsbook than you had ever seen in your life. The N.F.L. now has an official casino sponsor (Caesars) and partnerships with seven sports books. Nearly 60 million football bets were processed online in the United States last weekend — likely an all-time high — and the N.F.L. was probably thrilled about every single one of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multime