have a small collection of nonfungible tokens (NFTs). I’ll spare all of you the lengthy throat-clearing about cryptocurrency, provenance and some litany of explainer clauses and just say that an NFT is more or less a digital deed that says you own something unique on the internet. To date, NFTs have mostly taken the form of digital images, which, in turn, can sell for tens of millions of dollars in the same way that a painting might sell for tens of millions of dollars at an art auction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/20/opinion/20kang/20kang-articleLarge.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/20/opinion/20kang/20kang-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/20/opinion/20kang/20kang-jumbo.png', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/20/opinion/20kang/20kang-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1080, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/20/opinion/20kang/20kang-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/20/opinion/20kang/20kang-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/20/opinion/20kang/20kang-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why My NFT Toad Brought Me Joy', 'kicker': 'Jay Caspian Kang', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonfungible Tokens (NFTs)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'internal-sub-only', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-20T19:27:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Caspian Kang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': 'Caspian', 'lastname': 'Kang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/20973621-b46c-5323-8ace-1b0b52a13902', 'word_count': 2139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20973621-b46c-5323-8ace-1b0b52a13902'}, {'abstract': 'Wokmon funnels the flame from a gas burner, focusing the heat on the pan for better wok hei.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/20/dining/wokmon-wok-gas-stove.html', 'snippet': 'Wokmon funnels the flame from a gas burner, focusing the heat on the pan for better wok hei.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Glen Lee, an actor and inventor with a passion for cooking Chinese food, decided to try to make his home stove behave like a restaurant wok stove, with extra high heat concentrated at the base of a traditional round-bottom steel wok. He succeeded after many years and finally introduced the two-part gadget for gas stoves in 2019, with a curve-sided ring to focus the fire and a base to place over it to hold the pan. Originally the set came in a small and a medium size, for burners up to 3 3/4 inches in diameter. He has just introduced a large size for burners 4 to 5 1/2 inches. All the rings come with sets of legs; depending on the configuration of your burners and grates, setting them up securely can be tricky. To me it’s best if you cook with a wok frequently enough to want to keep one of these installed on a burner at all times.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-wok/20Burner-wok-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-wok/20Burner-wok-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-wok/20Burner-wok-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-wok/20Burner-wok-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-wok/20Burner-wok-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-wok/20Burner-wok-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-wok/20Burner-wok-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Wok Adapter That Really Works', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Blast: This Wok Adapter Is a Real Treat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-20T19:31:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76f2e9ee-8850-5ff2-9061-9242ffcc012c', 'word_count': 193, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76f2e9ee-8850-5ff2-9061-9242ffcc012c'}, {'abstract': 'The FoodxFilm Festival, supported by the United Nations Food Systems Summit, puts the focus on documentary film.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/20/dining/food-x-film-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The FoodxFilm Festival, supported by the United Nations Food Systems Summit, puts the focus on documentary film.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FoodxFilm Festival is a new global, virtual festival of food-related documentary films and series, mostly full-length, that examine social issues, agriculture, the environment, the sea and the future of food. It starts on Sunday and continues on Oct. 2 and 3. Among the films are “The Taste of Desire,” a global look at oysters; “When Tomatoes Met Wagner” about Greek farmers in a small village; and David Chang’s series made by Morgan Neville, “The Next Thing You Eat.” Several panels to discuss food issues will be part of the festival. It is free of charge but registration is required. The films and panels are available to stream on the festival’s website  for 24 hours after they appear. The festival was created by the Guild of Future Architects, in association with the Rockefeller Foundation, and is supported by the United Nations Food Systems Summit, the World Food Forum, and Good Food for All.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-film/20burner-film-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-film/20burner-film-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-film/20burner-film-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-film/20burner-film-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-film/20burner-film-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-film/20burner-film-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-film/20burner-film-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Festival Presents Food on Film', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To View: A New Festival Puts Food on Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-20T19:32:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e0a2367-c0fa-5586-825d-2964a6a04eb8', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e0a2367-c0fa-5586-825d-2964a6a04eb8'}, {'abstract': 'Soups, sandwiches and that chocolate chip cookie are all here in “Maman: The Cookbook,” from the downtown Manhattan cafe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/20/dining/maman-cookbook.html', 'snippet': 'Soups, sandwiches and that chocolate chip cookie are all here in “Maman: The Cookbook,” from the downtown Manhattan cafe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I fell in love with Maman, a cafe and bakery dressed in toile de Jouy, from the minute it opened on the edge of SoHo in 2014. And when the cookbook by the owners Elisa Marshall and Benjamin Sormonte, written with Lauren Salkeld, crossed my desk I decided that if it had the nutty chocolate chip cookie recipe and it worked, the book was worth recommending. Yes, and yes. The thick batter is not so easy to assemble but the effort is worth the results: more than a dozen giant cookies (more than four inches in diameter). I made smaller ones with half the batter and they turned out fine. This is not a book to consult for dinner; most of the recipes, like the cafe itself, which now has several locations in New York and Canada, suit lunch, all-day dining and light suppers. Salads and sandwiches abound. I also recommend the red wine, mushroom and onion soup; the cherry tomato, caramelized onion and feta tart; the olive oil-blood orange loaf; and the spiced turmeric tea.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-book/20Burner-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-book/20Burner-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 776}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-book/20Burner-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-book/20Burner-book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1650, 'width': 1275, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-book/20Burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-book/20Burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-book/20Burner-book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Maman Reveals Its Cookie Formula in New Cookbook', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Bake: Maman Reveals All In New Cookbook', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Maman (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Maman: The Cookbook (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Elisa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sormonte, Benjamin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Salkeld, Lauren', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-20T19:32:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/31693799-87e9-5ad1-9fbd-9018cbcd58db', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31693799-87e9-5ad1-9fbd-9018cbcd58db'}, {'abstract': 'Café Sabarsky will now offer meal kits for takeaway, featuring Austro-Hungarian favorites like chicken paprikash and beef goulash.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/20/dining/cafe-sabarsky-to-go.html', 'snippet': 'Café Sabarsky will now offer meal kits for takeaway, featuring Austro-Hungarian favorites like chicken paprikash and beef goulash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Café Sabarsky in the Neue Galerie is offering food to take away for the first time. Meal kits serving two, generously, offer specialties from Austria, Hungary and Germany, like chicken paprikash and beef goulash, both with spätzle ($58 each); and roasted bratwurst with sauerkraut and potatoes, and Bavarian sausage with a pretzel ($36 each). There’s also a vegetarian spätzle dish with mushrooms ($36). Christopher Engel, the executive chef, prepares all the ingredients and provides instructions for reheating and assembly. Desserts ($18 to $20), also for two, are apple strudel, Sacher torte and a layered nougat Mozart cake with pistachio and chocolate. Whole cakes are also sold to go. As an optional alternative to the usual takeout containers, the museum is selling handsome reusable double-layered stainless steel tiffins ($28) in which the meals can be packed. Ordering is by phone, 212-288-0665, or email, cafe@neuegalerie.org, 24 hours in advance. Pickup is available during Café Sabarsky hours, Thursday through Sunday 9 a.m. to 9 p.m. and Monday 9 a.m. to 6 p.m.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-Cafe/20Burner-Cafe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-Cafe/20Burner-Cafe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-Cafe/20Burner-Cafe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-Cafe/20Burner-Cafe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-Cafe/20Burner-Cafe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-Cafe/20Burner-Cafe-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20Burner-Cafe/20Burner-Cafe-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Austrian Comfort Food to Go', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Serve: Austrian Comfort Food Ready to Take Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe Sabarsky (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-20T19:34:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25b41e03-b01e-54c5-94af-672dfc88b110', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25b41e03-b01e-54c5-94af-672dfc88b110'}, {'abstract': 'A cidery in Michigan, Virtue Cider, now offers single-varietals in a quarterly subscription service.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/20/dining/drinks/virtue-cider-society.html', 'snippet': 'A cidery in Michigan, Virtue Cider, now offers single-varietals in a quarterly subscription service.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As cider makers continue to hone their craft, food-friendly options have increased exponentially. Poured into stemware, the golden drinks shine at dinner; they are less filling than beer and lower in alcohol than wine. One way to explore a variety of ciders is with the new Cider Society subscription packages, offered quarterly, from Virtue Cider in Fennville, Mich.  The first one, for the fall season, has four bottles of the company’s new single-varietal ciders, a change of pace since most ciders are blends. Golden Russet, Spitz, Baldwin and Jonathan, all lightly sparkling and deliciously dry, have distinctive profiles. There’s a whisper of mellow sweetness in the Golden Russet and the Spitz, and the Baldwin suggests sauvignon blanc. Next up, the winter box will offer four ciders from a line called the Mitten Series, aged in bourbon and rye barrels.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-cider/20burner-cider-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-cider/20burner-cider-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-cider/20burner-cider-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-cider/20burner-cider-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1314, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-cider/20burner-cider-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-cider/20burner-cider-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/dining/20burner-cider/20burner-cider-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Join the Cider Club', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sip: Your Subscription For Cider Is Here', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cider', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fennville (Mich)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-20T19:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fcf0079f-a27e-5e27-b469-fc9b5748f5fb', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fcf0079f-a27e-5e27-b469-fc9b5748f5fb'}, {'abstract': 'The former Treasury secretary has attracted investment from Saudi Arabia’s sovereign wealth fund.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/20/us/politics/mnuchin-saudi-private-equity.html', 'snippet': 'The former Treasury secretary has attracted investment from Saudi Arabia’s sovereign wealth fund.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Steven Mnuchin has raised $2.5 billion at his new private equity fund, according to people familiar with the matter, attracting investments from sovereign wealth funds in the Middle East, including Saudi Arabia, where he traveled extensively as Treasury secretary.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/business/20dc-mnuchin-print/merlin_180681867_92292289-da7c-42d5-acd7-721fc8a562e9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/21/business/20dc-mnuchin-print/merlin_180681867_92292289-da7c-42d5-acd7-721fc8a562e9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/business/20dc-mnuchin-print/merlin_180681867_92292289-da7c-42d5-acd7-7