'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62107d07-5314-5969-b12d-21b22709ad81'}, {'abstract': 'In an interview, the actor discusses leaving “Chicago Med” for her soapy new Fox drama about a powerful Black community on Martha’s Vineyard. “I can carry a show,” she said. “It’s time.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/arts/television/yaya-dacosta-our-kind-of-people.html', 'snippet': 'In an interview, the actor discusses leaving “Chicago Med” for her soapy new Fox drama about a powerful Black community on Martha’s Vineyard. “I can carry a show,” she said. “It’s time.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'After six seasons playing the nurse April Sexton on the hit NBC medical drama “Chicago Med,” Yaya DaCosta was contemplating her future in the “Chicago” franchise earlier this spring when she received an auspicious offer. She was given the opportunity to lead Fox’s “Our Kind of People,” a soapy new drama centering on the rich and powerful Black elite in Oak Bluffs on Martha’s Vineyard, and she was ready for it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/arts/21DACOSTA1/merlin_194434251_c322fd18-1a06-4b84-8058-be8a8aaa2c79-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/21/arts/21DACOSTA1/merlin_194434251_c322fd18-1a06-4b84-8058-be8a8aaa2c79-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 486}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/arts/21DACOSTA1/merlin_194434251_c322fd18-1a06-4b84-8058-be8a8aaa2c79-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 829, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/arts/21DACOSTA1/merlin_194434251_c322fd18-1a06-4b84-8058-be8a8aaa2c79-superJumbo.jpg', 'heig