f_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ca3264e-6abe-56e4-b238-848551bae3b7', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ca3264e-6abe-56e4-b238-848551bae3b7'}, {'abstract': 'After a record-breaking single, a tentative EP, a public coming out and another newsworthy smash, the 22-year-old pop sensation offers a fuller view of his inner world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/arts/music/lil-nas-x-montero-review.html', 'snippet': 'After a record-breaking single, a tentative EP, a public coming out and another newsworthy smash, the 22-year-old pop sensation offers a fuller view of his inner world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lil Nas X, the gleefully queer 22-year-old pop star and savvy digital trickster, often cuts an impossibly confident figure in public. Red carpets and awards show stages have lately become international showcases for his impishly androgynous imagination. On social media — his own personal amusement park — his deft retorts to purer-than-thou pearl-clutchers and homophobic haters seem so effortless, they prompt a modern philosophical question: What’s the sound of one hand clapping back?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/arts/21lilnas-review1/merlin_195042618_1aae6081-44cc-4921-b0ce-986a67f78f63-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/22/arts/21lilnas-review1/merlin_195042618_1aae6081-44cc-4921-b0ce-986a67f78f63-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 825}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/arts/21lilnas-review1/merlin_195042618_1aae6081-44cc-4921-b0ce-986a67f78f63-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 745, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/arts/21lilnas-review1/merlin_195042618_1aae6081-44cc-4921-b0ce-986a67f78f63-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1490, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/arts/21lilnas-review1/merlin_195042618_1aae6081-44cc-4921-b0ce-986a67f78f63-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/22/arts/21lilnas-review1/merlin_195042618_1aae6081-44cc-4921-b0ce-986a67f78f63-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/22/arts/21lilnas-review1/merlin_195042618_1aae6081-44cc-4921-b0ce-986a67f78f63-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lil Nas X Reveals Himself on ‘Montero’', 'kicker': 'Album Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pop Sensation Slips Off the Glitzy Public Armor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lil Nas X (Rapper)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Montero (Album)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-21T16:57:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lindsay Zoladz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lindsay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zoladz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b4e920e-15ea-5823-9b1c-ae74d1d4f9a2', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b4e920e-15ea-5823-9b1c-ae74d1d4f9a2'}, {'abstract': 'Spending more on children is a very good idea.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/opinion/child-tax-credit-poverty.html', 'snippet': 'Spending more on children is a very good idea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans love rags-to-riches stories, tales of people who transcended childhood poverty to achieve adult success. Unless you’re totally oblivious to reality, however, you surely realize that such stories are the exceptions, not the rule. The disadvantages of growing up in poverty — poor nutrition, poor health care, an impoverished environment, the cognitive burden that goes along with never having enough money — can and often do hobble children for the rest of their lives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/opinion/21krugman-news/21krugman-news-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/21/opinion/21krugman-news/21krugman-news-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/opinion/21krugman-news/21krugman-news-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/opinion/21krugman-news/21krugman-news-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/opinion/21krugman-news/21krugman-news-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width'