imes', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Transcript: Ezra Klein Interviews Leslie Reagan', 'kicker': 'The Ezra Klein Show', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-09-21T17:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c80917f5-0b3a-53f3-8a5a-432c9eb27ca3', 'word_count': 9158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c80917f5-0b3a-53f3-8a5a-432c9eb27ca3'}, {'abstract': 'The broad package of new curbs to executive power is a response to numerous norms of self-restraint that former President Donald J. Trump violated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/us/house-democrats-executive-power.html', 'snippet': 'The broad package of new curbs to executive power is a response to numerous norms of self-restraint that former President Donald J. Trump violated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'House Democratic leaders introduced on Tuesday a much-anticipated package of proposed new limits on executive power, launching a post-Trump push to strengthen checks on the presidency that they hope will compare to the overhauls that followed the Watergate scandal and the Vietnam War.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'House Democrats introduced the ‘Protecting Our Democracy Act.’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidents and Presidency (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schiff, Adam B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-21T17:10:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/279602b3-a4d2-59f4-87df-59b8877e2bc6', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/279602b3-a4d2-59f4-87df-59b8877e2bc6'}, {'abstract': 'A little empathy goes a long way, and people are going to judge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/21/well/family/pregnancy-after-40.html', 'snippet': 'A little empathy goes a long way, and people are going to judge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time a stranger mistook me for the grandmother of my own child, I was in an airport, hauling my 2-year-old to a connecting flight. I was purchasing a bottle of water; the baby was having a tantrum. I put her on the floor to let her shriek and calmly made my purchase. The clerk gave me a sororal smile and said: “Grandchildren are a handful, that’s for sure. I’ve got four of my own!”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/well/21well-old-mom/21well-old-mom-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/21/well/21well-old-mom/21well-old-mom-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/well/21well-old-mom/21well-old-mom-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/well/21well-old-mom/21well-old-mom-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1166, 'width': 1750, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy'