and are sure to brighten up your space in more ways than one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 2010s, when homes began to double as backdrops for social media posts, the branded candle, or evidence thereof, became ubiquitous. Maybe it was a Le Labo Santal 26 burning serenely alongside a neat stack of fashion books. Maybe it was an already-spent Diptyque variety, the empty glass holder now filled with makeup brushes and perched on the corner of a bathroom sink. Now modern classics, these candles are still around, and still smell as good as ever, but there’s a newer crop of options that are, well, weirder.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/t-magazine/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/21/t-magazine/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/t-magazine/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/t-magazine/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/21/t-magazine/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I/21tmag-weird-candles-slide-TJ5I-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 