ris-future-pandemic-funding.html', 'snippet': 'The new fund was established to address a range of issues like disease surveillance, vaccine development and health care worker support in order to counter future biological threats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While President Biden gathered with heads of state for a Covid-19 summit, Vice President Kamala Harris on Wednesday announced that the United States will contribute at least $250 million to a new global health security fund that the administration hopes will raise $10 billion to fight future pandemics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Harris announces $250 million in global funding to fight future pandemics.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coronavirus (2019-nCoV)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Kamala D', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-22T20:14:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin and Elian Peltier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peltier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a254ea48-6a22-5372-afc6-face20a718fa', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a254ea48-6a22-5372-afc6-face20a718fa'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Morrison, the poet laureate of lost films, turns the story of footage found near Iceland into a history of a slice of Soviet cinema.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/22/movies/the-village-detective-a-song-cycle-review.html', 'snippet': 'Bill Morrison, the poet laureate of lost films, turns the story of footage found near Iceland into a history of a slice of Soviet cinema.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The main title of this movie could be referring to two different people. The first would be Fyodor Ivanovich Aniskin, the avuncular hero of a banal 1969 Soviet film, played by the frequently avuncular actor Mikhail Zharov. Consulting on a case in which a musician, new to his hamlet, complains of a purloined accordion, Aniskin notes that the man does not yet understand the values of their small town.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/23/arts/23village-detective/merlin_194795601_0c8dd12d-a18f-4a27-88a6-f8b6905d7582-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/23/arts/23village-detective/merlin_194795601_0c8dd12d-a18f-4a27-88a6-f8b6905d7582-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/23/arts/23village-detective/merlin_194795601_0c8dd12d-a18f-4a27-88a6-f8b6905d7582-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/23/arts/23village-detective/merlin_194795601_0c8dd12d-a18f-4a27-88a6-f8b6905d7582-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/23/arts/23village-detective/23village-detective-thumbSt