ect', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-23T00:40:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Weisman, Emily Cochrane and Jim Tankersley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weisman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cochrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tankersley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/274dd678-6d71-54d5-a256-26bf9a9aee50', 'word_count': 1556, 'uri': 'nyt://article/274dd678-6d71-54d5-a256-26bf9a9aee50'}, {'abstract': 'I’ve seen it happen time and again. Missing white women and girls receive outsize media coverage when other missing people receive none.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/22/opinion/petito-missing-person-cases.html', 'snippet': 'I’ve seen it happen time and again. Missing white women and girls receive outsize media coverage when other missing people receive none.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The breathless coverage of the disappearance and apparent killing of Gabrielle Petito has played out in a virtual — and sometimes literal — split screen alongside images of mounted officers in Texas swinging long reins like whips while herding Haitian migrants. That startling contrast forces us once again to wrestle with a crucial question: What kinds of people, in what kinds of bodies, with what kinds of lineage do we value?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': N