re indelible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/23/movies/most-beautiful-boy-in-the-world-review.html', 'snippet': 'The 1971 film “Death in Venice” showcased the delicate androgyny of Bjorn Andresen’s face and form, but the changes it wrought on his life are indelible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Almost 30 years ago I interviewed the onetime child actor Bill Mumy, who was about 40 by then. He had played Will Robinson on “Lost in Space” when he was a kid and was now enjoying a creatively prosperous adulthood. Which has not often been the case for child actors. Citing himself and Jodie Foster, he insisted that what made a difference for them was preparation — professional training at an early age.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/23most-beautiful-boy-pix/merlin_194792541_17d63f43-4e56-4c16-b599-508a1e2421a8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/23most-beautiful-boy-pix/merlin_194792541_17d63f43-4e56-4c16-b599-508a1e2421a8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/23most-beautiful-boy-pix/merlin_194792541_17d63f43-4e56-4c16-b599-508a1e2421a8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 699, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/23most-beautiful-boy-pix/merlin_194792541_17d63f43-4e56-4c16-b599-508a1e2421a8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1398, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/23most-beautiful-boy-pix/23most-beautiful-boy-pix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/23most-beautiful-boy-pix/23most-beautiful-boy-pix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/23most-beautiful-boy-pix/23most-beautiful-boy-pix-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Most Beautiful Boy in the World’ Review: A Cautionary Tale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Perfect Beauty Can Be a Beast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Content Type: Personal Profile', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Actors and Actresses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Most Beautiful Boy in the World (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindstrom, Kristina (Filmmaker)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Petri, Kristian (1956- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andresen, Bjorn (1955- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Visconti, Luchino', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-23T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/65920ccf-c917-5d5e-b00c-33a2db5fb1ca', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65920ccf-c917-5d5e-b00c-33a2db5fb1ca'}, {'abstract': 'The latest entry in the children’s franchise pits an eclectic team of progressive ponies against a fear mongering demagogue and the prejudices of their communities at large', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/23/movies/my-little-pony-a-new-generation-review.html', 'snippet': 'The latest entry in the children’s franchise pits an eclectic team of progressive ponies against a fear mongering demagogue and the prejudices of their communities at large', 'lead_paragraph': 'Out with the hand drawn-animated ponies, in with their creepily-anthropomorphized, digitally-animated brethren: the “new generation,” if you will, which includes not only ponies but Pegasi and unicorns from all over Equestria. This “My Little Pony” movie takes a contemporary spin on the franchise’s tot-friendly tenets of love and friendship by staging a political awakening about tolerance, prejudice, even fascism — sweetened, of course, with musical numbers, cutesy gags, and pastel vistas.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/mylittlepony1/merlin_194843295_f1381882-186a-4589-bb51-3cfb240a7a50-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 251, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/mylittlepony1/merlin_194843295_f1381882-186a-4589-bb51-3cfb240a7a50-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 251}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/24/arts/mylittlepony1/merlin_194843295_f1381882-186a-4589-bb51-3cfb240a7a50-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':