rts/design/joe-minter-gees-bend-souls-grown-deep.html', 'snippet': 'From Birmingham to Gee’s Bend, the Souls Grown Deep Foundation is directly investing in Alabama communities where artists and quilters live, work — and struggle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BIRMINGHAM, Ala. — “I’m the conjurer of all my ancestors, 400 years of African people in America,” said Joe Minter, surveying the dense outdoor environment of artworks he has forged from refuse over the past 32 years across his half-acre yard, facing two of the largest African-American cemeteries in the south. Nodding to the tombstones, he added, “they have given me the privilege of being their spokesman.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/26/arts/26minter-1/merlin_193969233_331c24e6-2e59-4b6b-8492-48f63c9f524c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/26/arts/26minter-1/merlin_193969233_331c24e6-2e59-4b6b-8492-48f63c9f524c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 895}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/26/arts/26minter-1/merlin_193969233_331c24e6-2e59-4b6b-8492-48f63c9f524c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/26/arts/26minter-1/merlin_193969233_331c24e6-2e59-4b6b-8492-48f63c9f524c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1373, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/26/arts/26minter-1/26minter-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 