ported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/105c8b63-d24f-57b3-b223-4714c9c529b7', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/105c8b63-d24f-57b3-b223-4714c9c529b7'}, {'abstract': 'Sixty million people are eligible to vote in the German national election on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/26/world/what-time-results-germany-election-polls.html', 'snippet': 'Sixty million people are eligible to vote in the German national election on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sixty million people are eligible to vote in the German national election on Sunday. There won’t be a new government that night, or the next day — it could take the rival parties weeks or even months to settle on a coalition with a parliamentary majority. But the ballots are tallied quickly, and the new shape of Germany’s political landscape is likely to be visible within hours.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What to watch for on Sunday.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2021-09-26T12:53:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher F. Schuetze', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Schuetze', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34318038-1734-5215-ac8b-fbeba77bc177', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34318038-1734-5215-ac8b-fbeba77bc177'}, {'abstract': 'The emerging brand Sunnei went all-in on goggles on Milan Fashion Week’s third day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/26/style/goggles-sunglasses.html', 'snippet': 'The emerging brand Sunnei went all-in on goggles on Milan Fashion Week’s third day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fashion W