— The Biden administration plans to publish a proposed rule on Tuesday in hopes of preserving Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals, or DACA, a program that has protected hundreds of thousands of undocumented young adults from deportation and allowed them to legally work in the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/27/us/politics/27dc-daca/merlin_193373211_8381c5ba-2695-4376-b198-8b7588aecc12-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/27/us/politics/27dc-daca/merlin_193373211_8381c5ba-2695-4376-b198-8b7588aecc12-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/27/us/politics/27dc-daca/merlin_193373211_8381c5ba-2695-4376-b198-8b7588aecc12-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/27/us/politics/27dc-daca/merlin_193373211_8381c5ba-2695-4376-b198-8b7588aecc12-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/27/us/politics/27dc-daca/merlin_193373211_8381c5ba-2695-4376-b198-8b7588aecc12-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/27/us/politics/27dc-daca/merlin_193373211_8381c5ba-2695-4376-b198-8b7588aecc12-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/27/us/politics/27dc-daca/merlin_193373211_8381c5ba-2695-4376-b198-8b7588aecc12-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Biden Administration Moves to Protect Undocumented Young Adults', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Administration Is Taking Step On Protection For ‘Dreamers’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dream Act (Development, Relief and Education for Minors Act)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizenship and Naturalization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-27T20:37:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miriam Jordan and Eileen Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miriam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jordan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eileen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e70de867-1952-5845-96b7-4e30f595c3e1', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e70de867-1952-5845-96b7-4e30f595c3e1'}, {'abstract': 'Kettl, a tea shop and retailer in Greenpoint, features tea to-go as well as a variety of tea-driven sweets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/27/dining/tea-shop-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Kettl, a tea shop and retailer in Greenpoint, features tea to-go as well as a variety of tea-driven sweets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year Zach and Minami Mangan, importers of tea from Japan, dipped their toes into the retail market with a Kettl stand in the tiny mall on the Bowery in NoHo. Its success has now led them to add a graciously serene store in a part of Greenpoint, Brooklyn, that’s become a hub for food. Shelves at the new store, also called Kettl, are lined with packages of teas and handmade pottery bowls, cups and teapots, some made by Ms. Mangan. There’s a communal table in the middle and, in the rear, a concrete tasting counter; in the front is a takeaway window, which is comparable to the Bowery spot. The Mangans have brought in a matcha grinder from Japan; Mr. Mangan also does some of his own roasting. And at this location they’ve added a menu of tea-driven sweets, including a chestnut Mont Blanc cake with matcha, delicate mousses, a baroque layered parfait, and excellent matcha chocolate chip cookies that play up the chocolaty taste of the tea. The confections are made by Chika Hanyu, a pastry chef nearby. “Our expertise is tea so we didn’t want to get involved in running a kitchen,” Mr. Mangan said.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-tea/merlin_195213207_06a431e6-402b-4f8a-92e6-a57a63b26d2f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-tea/merlin_195213207_06a431e6-402b-4f8a-92e6-a57a63b26d2f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-tea/merlin_195213207_06a431e6-402b-4f8a-92e6-a57a63b26d2f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-tea/merlin_195213207_06a431e6-402b-4f8a-92e6-a57a63b26d2f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-tea/merlin_195213207_06a431e6-402b-4f8a-92e6-a57a63b26d2f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-tea/merlin_195213207_06a431e6-402b-4f8a-92e6-a57a63b26d2f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-tea/merlin_195213207_06a431e6-402b-4f8a-92e6-a57a63b26d2f-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Destination for Tea Lovers in Brooklyn', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Shop: New Destination For Tea in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenpoint (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kettl Tea Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-27T20:42:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/272df96e-2142-5abc-b892-50a50ff84508', 'word_count': 233, 'uri': 'nyt://article/272df96e-2142-5abc-b892-50a50ff84508'}, {'abstract': 'The Food Network & Cooking Channel New York City Wine & Food Festival returns for in-person dinners and tastings next month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/27/dining/nyc-food-festival-asian-night-market.html', 'snippet': 'The Food Network & Cooking Channel New York City Wine & Food Festival returns for in-person dinners and tastings next month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The annual Food Network & Cooking Channel New York City Wine & Food Festival benefiting Gods Love We Deliver and the Food Bank for New York City returns to in-person events this year (with Covid protocols observed), Oct. 14 through 17. Among the scores of dinners, tastings, cooking demonstrations and wine events is a new Asian night market in Times Square. Led by the Food Network personalities Jet Tila and Molly Yeh, at least a dozen stands will be assembled for the walk-around street food fest, among them Poova Bavishi of Malai, Ly Nguyen and Patrick Lin of Em Vietnamese, and Tatsuya Sekiguchi of Tatsu Dallas.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Night/27Burner-Night-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Night/27Burner-Night-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Night/27Burner-Night-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Night/27Burner-Night-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Night/27Burner-Night-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Night/27Burner-Night-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Night/27Burner-Night-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Asian Night Market for a Returning New York City Food Festival', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sample: Asian Night Market For Wine and Food Event', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food Network', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cooking Channel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-27T20:46:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7208a98e-85db-58d8-9a63-1475c83e6643', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7208a98e-85db-58d8-9a63-1475c83e6643'}, {'abstract': "What started out as an April Fools’ gag is now a one-of-a-kind jarred pickle from Katz's Delicatessen and Hendrick’s Gin.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/27/dining/hendricks-gin-katzs-pickles.html', 'snippet': "What started out as an April Fools’ gag is now a one-of-a-kind jarred pickle from Katz's Delicatessen and Hendrick’s Gin.", 'lead_paragraph': 'A pastrami sandwich with a martini alongside is a good idea. Make them with pastrami from Katz’s Delicatessen and Hendrick’s Gin, and you can tie them together with a special edition of Katz’s pickles brined with the juniper berries, cubeb berries and coriander used in Hendrick’s, a gin famously infused with cucumber, the key pickle ingredient. The collaboration between Jake Dell, the owner of Katz’s, and Lesley Gracie, the master distiller at Hendrick’s, came about as an April Fools’ gag. This year, Hendrick’s posted a recipe for gin-infused pickles on Instagram without any intention of selling them. But the response was such that they ended up working with Katz’s. The pickles are in the half-sour category, barely; they still have the fresh green crunch of a new pickle. The brine conveys enough juniper so a splash of it along with a few slices of the pickle will enhance that martini.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-pickles/27burner-pickles-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 340, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-pickles/27burner-pickles-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 340}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-pickles/27burner-pickles-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 581, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-pickles/27burner-pickles-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1162, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-pickles/27burner-pickles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-pickles/27burner-pickles-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27burner-pickles/27burner-pickles-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Institutions Come Together for a Briny Collaboration', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Savor: Two Institutions Form A Briny Collaboration', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gin (Liquor)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Katz's Delicatessen (Manhattan, NY)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-27T20:48:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14c234fa-b924-584a-93d5-270dec6d92af', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14c234fa-b924-584a-93d5-270dec6d92af'}, {'abstract': 'The creamery is starting to turn out even more of its high-quality cheeses thanks to several copper-lined vats from France.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/27/dining/jasper-hill-farm-french-cheese.html', 'snippet': 'The creamery is starting to turn out even more of its high-quality cheeses thanks to several copper-lined vats from France.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mateo Kehler, the cheese maker who owns Jasper Hill Farm in northern Vermont with his brother, Andy, has just eliminated a lot of backbreaking work for the esteemed creamery. He bought a few big copper-lined vats that a Comté cheese maker in the Jura region of eastern France no longer uses because they have transitioned to larger equipment. The secondhand vats, which can handle 3,000 liters (3,170 quarts) of milk, replace Mr. Kehler’s smaller vessels. Most importantly they are engineered so the curds are transferred to a vacuum system by gravity to the lower level of the creamery where they are pressed and formed, and no longer require the hands-on chore of moving the curds manually. “It’s automated, easier to clean, there’s no waste, we can make more cheese and they will be more consistent,” he said. The Alpha Tolman, Whitney and Highlander are the varieties being produced with the new equipment.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Cheese/27Burner-Cheese-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Cheese/27Burner-Cheese-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Cheese/27Burner-Cheese-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Cheese/27Burner-Cheese-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Cheese/27Burner-Cheese-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Cheese/27Burner-Cheese-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-Cheese/27Burner-Cheese-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cheese Making at Jasper Hill Farm Gets a French Advantage', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Produce: Cheese Making Gets A French Advantage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Jasper Hill Farm (Greensboro, Vt)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-27T20:50:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae6891d2-b185-520f-9167-e77ffb1aa836', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae6891d2-b185-520f-9167-e77ffb1aa836'}, {'abstract': 'In her new memoir, Dorothy Kalins passes on the lessons she picked up while rubbing elbows with world-class chefs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/27/dining/dorothy-kalins-memoir-saveur.html', 'snippet': 'In her new memoir, Dorothy Kalins passes on the lessons she picked up while rubbing elbows with world-class chefs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to kitchen smarts, Dorothy Kalins, a founder and the former editor in chief of Saveur magazine, and the editor of several cookbooks, deserves bragging rights. “The Kitchen Whisperers,” her new kitchen memoir is populated with many of the culinary names she worked with over the decades, like Colman Andrews, Marcella Hazan, Michael Anthony and Anita Lo, all of whom enhanced her own expertise. Through her eyes and lively prose, they provide the book’s compelling common-sense approach to food that will easily resonate with experienced cooks and should bolster the confidence of novices. There are only a few of what you might consider recipes, in paragraph form, but after absorbing what Ms. Kalins recounts you may find you have less need for them.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-book/27Burner-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 871, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-book/27Burner-book-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 871}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-book/27Burner-book-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 706, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-book/27Burner-book-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1412, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-book/27Burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-book/27Burner-book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-book/27Burner-book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Founding Editor of Saveur Shares What She Learned', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Learn: A Saveur Founder Shares With the Class', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Saveur (Magazine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-27T20:53:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68373139-39dc-5e43-afa2-2f763e6013d6', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68373139-39dc-5e43-afa2-2f763e6013d6'}, {'abstract': '“Majolica Mania” at the Bard Graduate Center explores the nation’s obsession with the highly decorative earthenware.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/27/dining/vibrant-pottery-filled-with-whimsy.html', 'snippet': '“Majolica Mania” at the Bard Graduate Center explores the nation’s obsession with the highly decorative earthenware.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From 1850 until the 1920s, highly decorative Majolica ceramics were nothing short of a craze. Makers were initially inspired by Italian Renaissance maiolica and French Palissy ware, and the molded earthenware — made in England and the United States — was fanciful yet practical, whimsical yet drawn from nature. An exhibition of 380 pieces on four floors, including many designed for serving oysters, asparagus, celery, berries and tea, will be on display at the Bard Graduate Center on the Upper West Side from Sept. 24 to Jan. 2, 2022. It will then go to the Walters Art Museum in Baltimore (Feb. 27 to Aug. 7, 2022). In addition to pieces for serving food, there are purely ornamental items, like a life-size peacock. The fashion for Majolica died down with changing tastes and also the use of lead glazes in the manufacture.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-show/27Burner-show-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-show/27Burner-show-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-show/27Burner-show-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-show/27Burner-show-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1461, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-show/27Burner-show-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-show/27Burner-show-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/dining/27Burner-show/27Burner-show-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vibrant Pottery Filled With Whimsy', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Explore: Vibrant Pottery  Filled With Whimsy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bard Graduate Center for Studies in the Decorative Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-27T20:57:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf1695af-a228-50ea-9a68-de04a83ac213', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf1695af-a228-50ea-9a68-de04a83ac213'}, {'abstract': 'Rather than trying to make significant gains in the state, where Democrats have been increasingly ascendant in recent years, Republicans appear to be trying to bolster their existing congressional delegation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/27/us/politics/texas-congress-map-republicans.html', 'snippet': 'Rather than trying to make significant gains in the state, where Democrats have been increasingly ascendant in recent years, Republicans appear to be trying to bolster their existing congressional delegation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans in the Texas Legislature proposed a new congressional map on Monday that would preserve the party’s advantage in the state’s delegation to Washington amid booming population growth spurred by communities of color.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/27/