r bone, only those delicate trailing tentacles studded with nematocysts, tiny tubes filled with venom. These are essentially projectiles that “act as a hypodermic delivery device,” explains Angel Yanagihara, a biochemist at the University of Hawaii at Manoa who, after barely surviving a box jellyfish sting 24 years ago, has devoted her career to studying the mechanics of her near killer.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '60', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/28/t-magazine/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/28/t-magazine/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/28/t-magazine/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/28/t-magazine/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/28/t-magazine/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/28/t-magazine/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/28/t-magazine/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy/28tmag-eatingmonsters-slide-LQCG-copy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Does It Mean to Eat What You Fear?', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Monster \t Within', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jellyfish', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Octopus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Park Chan-Wook', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-28T13:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan and Anthony Cotsifas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotsifas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2add3a09-90d6-51a4-9db6-68f4e5222fac', 'word_count': 2239, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2add3a09-90d6-51a4-9db6-68f4e5222fac'}, {'abstract': 'As M.L.B. front offices get more and more corporate, titles have steadily inflated. Yesterday’s general manager is today’s president of baseball operations … or chief baseball officer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/28/sports/baseball/e