ss in the early 1960s with catchy novelty songs, as well as the occasional ballad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sue Thompson, who after more than a decade of moderate success as a country singer found pop stardom in the early 1960s with hook-laden novelty hits like “Sad Movies (Make Me Cry)” and “Norman,” died on Thursday at the home of her daughter and caregiver, Julie Jennings, in Pahrump, Nev. She was 96.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/obituaries/28thompson1-print1/merlin_195486024_83663ee4-2a20-459d-a4ad-478e249cb3da-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 727, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/obituaries/28thompson1-print1/merlin_195486024_83663ee4-2a20-459d-a4ad-478e249cb3da-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 727}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/obituaries/28thompson1-print1/merlin_195486024_83663ee4-2a20-459d-a4ad-478e249cb3da-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 845, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/obituaries/28thompson1-print1/merlin_195486024_83663ee4-2a20-459d-a4ad-478e249cb3da-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1690, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/obituaries/28thompson1-print1/merlin_195486024_83663ee4-2a20-459d-a4ad-478e249cb3da-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/29/obituaries/28thompson1-print1/merlin_195486024_83663ee4-2a20-459d-a4ad-478e249cb3da-t