e, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Convicts Magazine  In Paris of Racist Insults', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obono, Daniele', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Valeurs Actuelles (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery (Historical)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-29T16:44:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aurelien Breeden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aurelien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Breeden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af21171d-e1dc-56a5-b250-a4b136726512', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af21171d-e1dc-56a5-b250-a4b136726512'}, {'abstract': 'Rather than prioritizing confession and catharsis, today’s authors are focusing on the question of who gets to share their version of things and interrogating the form, along with themselves.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/29/t-magazine/memoirs-books-nonfiction-identity.html', 'snippet': 'Rather than prioritizing confession and catharsis, today’s authors are focusing on the question of who gets to share their version of things and interrogating the form, along with themselves.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN CERTAIN FAMILIES, there’s only room for one storyteller, and in mine, it was my grandfather. Grandpa O’Grady was always the hero of the anecdotes he told of his Depression-era childhood, which were about things like eating onions from the food donation box raw, out of hand, like apples, or driving his mother home from church after his father, who liked his whiskey, passed out in the pew. These stories, with their inevitable triumph-over-odds arc, were our firmament, but they also felt slightly apocryphal; when he told them, we were aware of witnessing a kind of performance, and that was probably why they gave us the giggles: the rhetorical flourish of certain repeated details — the juice of the raw onion “dribbling down his chin”; driving the car “in first gear the whole way.” At the same time, we sensed something real in his need to re-enact the same memories again and again in his effort to reconcile the genuine hardships of his past with a dissonant present embodied in his young grandchildren, indifferent to their apple-eating good fortune.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '80', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/t-magazine/29tmag-memoirs-slide-RTE3-copy/29tmag-memoirs-slide-RTE3-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/t-magazine/29tmag-memoirs-slide-RTE3-copy/29tmag-memoirs-slide-RTE3-copy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/t-magazine/29tmag-memoirs-slide-RTE3-copy/29tmag-memoirs-slide-RTE3-copy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/t-magazine/29tmag-memoirs-slide-RTE3-copy/29tmag-memoirs-slide-RTE3-copy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 1529, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': N