material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b6ee075-7018-54b7-8374-c95d37cf9c62', 'word_count': 1588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b6ee075-7018-54b7-8374-c95d37cf9c62'}, {'abstract': 'Sarah Tudzin started this Los Angeles band to show off her production work and find new clients. It turned into an outlet for her razor-sharp reflections on modern life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/29/arts/music/illuminati-hotties-let-me-do-one-more.html', 'snippet': 'Sarah Tudzin started this Los Angeles band to show off her production work and find new clients. It turned into an outlet for her razor-sharp reflections on modern life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The night before Sarah Tudzin filmed the music video for the first single from her band Illuminati Hotties’ new album, the director Katie Neuhof texted a picture of green, gelatinous glop cooking on her stove. In the middle of the clip for the exuberantly titled “Mmmoooaaaaayaya,” it was to be poured, Nickelodeon-style, onto Tudzin’s head.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/28hotties1/merlin_195413589_37f22c94-4f0c-4fb4-8cda-aa77292ca8e9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 506, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/28hotties1/merlin_195413589_37f22c94-4f0c-4fb4-8cda-aa77292ca8e9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 506}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/28hotties1/merlin_195413589_37f22c94-4f0c-4fb4-8cda-aa77292ca8e9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 863, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/28hotties1/merlin_195413589_37f22c94-4f0c-4fb4-8cda-aa77