nization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e54deddc-ce8d-5824-9600-dc337c76d5c2', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e54deddc-ce8d-5824-9600-dc337c76d5c2'}, {'abstract': 'Federal and state governments want to curb this widespread employment practice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/29/opinion/noncompete-agreement-workers.html', 'snippet': 'Federal and state governments want to curb this widespread employment practice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heidi Shierholz is not a fan of noncompete agreements, which many employers require new hires to sign. The contracts prohibit employees who quit from taking a job at a competitor for a period ranging from months to years. Often the stated justification is to protect a company’s business strategies from being shared with a rival. Shierholz, the new president of the Economic Policy Institute, says noncompete agreements rob workers of leverage against their bosses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/opinion/29coy/29coy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/opinion/29coy/29coy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/opinion/29coy/29coy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/opinion/29coy/29coy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/opinion/29coy/29coy-thum