': 'nyt://article/3aeeff8f-c7b8-55cf-9a56-cb27548803ee'}, {'abstract': 'When couples aren’t seeing eye to eye — and there seems to be more of these moments than usual lately — there are ways to redirect your energy to fight “well.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/30/style/how-to-fight-right.html', 'snippet': 'When couples aren’t seeing eye to eye — and there seems to be more of these moments than usual lately — there are ways to redirect your energy to fight “well.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dori Brail says she can tell when a fight is brewing with her wife of three years, Angie Peng. “I can feel it bubbling up,” said Ms. Brail, 41, a social work supervisor at a public defender’s office in New York. “The tone in our voices is different and our body language is stiffer and more defensive. Both of us need space when we’re upset, but at different times.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/fashion/07HowToFightFair/07HowToFightFair-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/07/fashion/07HowToFightFair/07HowToFightFair-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/fashion/07HowToFightFair/07HowToFightFair-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/fashion/07HowToFightFair/07HowToFightFair-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/07/fashion/07HowToFightFair/07HowToFightFair-thumbStandar