: 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/30/movies/the-addams-family-2-review.html', 'snippet': 'America’s creepiest family takes a road trip in this animated sequel, though their antics are far more kooky than spooky.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2019, the Addams family returned to the big screen for the first time since the 1990s, this time in animated form. The macabre clan, directly styled after Charles Addams’s original New Yorker cartoon characters and voiced by a star-studded cast, railed against normalcy and blew up a lot of stuff. Now, in a new sequel, they’re taking that show on the road. Like it’s predecessor, “The Addams Family 2” is more kooky than spooky, offering much more to young children than it may to the adults accompanying them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30addams-art/merlin_195501432_18b33d47-e193-4ebd-9510-5fdba4cce8b1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30addams-art/merlin_195501432_18b33d47-e193-4ebd-9510-5fdba4cce8b1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30addams-art/merlin_195501432_18b33d47-e193-4ebd-9510-5fdba4cce8b1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 553, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30addams-art/merlin_195501432_18b33d47-e193-4ebd-9510-5fdba4cce8b1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1105, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30addams-art/30addams-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30addams-art/30addams-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30addams-art/30addams-art-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Addams Family 2’ Review: Wednesday Goes West', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Addams Family 2 (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animated Films', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tiernan, Greg (Film Director)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vernon, Conrad', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brousseau, Laura', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-30T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lena Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/696cfe43-cf67-56f7-a525-2de5db554698', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/696cfe43-cf67-56f7-a525-2de5db554698'}, {'abstract': 'A loving documentary about a Pacific Northwest amphitheater, created by a long-ago natural catastrophe, that is a haven for concertgoers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/30/movies/review-enormous-the-gorge-story.html', 'snippet': 'A loving documentary about a Pacific Northwest amphitheater, created by a long-ago natural catastrophe, that is a haven for concertgoers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s the ideal place to experience live music? For some, a midsize hall with immaculate acoustics; for others, an intimate nightclub with a well-stocked bar; for others still, a clamorous, sweaty dive. For those who are able to get there, and who have an affinity with its vibe, the Gorge Amphitheater in George, Wash., with its scenic beauty and open-air sonics, is heaven.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/03/arts/03enormous-pix/merlin_195251334_a6fbbabf-f7ca-4e70-af03-4f148e1c168a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/10/03/arts/03enormous-pix/merlin_195251334_a6fbbabf-f7ca-4e70-af03-4f148e1c168a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/03/arts/03enormous-pix/merlin_195251334_a6fbbabf-f7ca-4e70-af03-4f148e1c168a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/03/arts/03enormous-pix/merlin_195251334_a6fbbabf-f7ca-4e70-af03-4f148e1c168a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/03/arts/03enormous-pix/03enormous-pix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/10/03/arts/03enormous-pix/03enormous-pix-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/10/03/arts/03enormous-pix/03enormous-pix-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Enormous: The Gorge Story’ Review: A Musical Paradise', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stadiums and Arenas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Enormous: The Gorge Story (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Nic (Filmmaker)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gorge Amphitheater (George, Wash)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-30T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/90c0be7a-46d5-5a23-a27b-4da8d35dd336', 'word_count': 290, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90c0be7a-46d5-5a23-a27b-4da8d35dd336'}, {'abstract': 'A family outing attracts mysterious, menacing uninvited guests in this grinding New Zealand thriller.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/30/movies/coming-home-in-the-dark-review.html', 'snippet': 'A family outing attracts mysterious, menacing uninvited guests in this grinding New Zealand thriller.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not infrequently, films set and shot in the Antipodes make a convincing case that one ought to never leave one’s house. Think of the scenarios of “Wake In Fright” (kangaroos and lunatics running amok), “Picnic at Hanging Rock” (girls-school adventurers disappear), “A Cry in the Dark” (dingo, baby). Directed by James Ashcroft from a script he wrote with Eli Kent (based on a short story by Owen Marshall), “Coming Home in the Dark” doesn’t take long in demonstrating that sometimes a day trip to high New Zealand spaces is not worth the views.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/arts/coming1/merlin_195188481_87dc9593-3e6a-47a8-8dc4-4464e1f7231f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/29/arts/coming1/merlin_195188481_87dc9593-3e6a-47a8-8dc4-4464e1f7231f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/arts/coming1/merlin_195188481_87dc9593-3e6a-47a8-8dc4-4464e1f7231f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/arts/coming1/merlin_195188481_87dc9593-3e6a-47a8-8dc4-4464e1f7231f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/arts/coming1/coming1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2021/09/29/arts/coming1/coming1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/29/arts/coming1/coming1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Coming Home in the Dark’ Review: No Picnic', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Coming Home in the Dark (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ashcroft, James (1978- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2021-09-30T11:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0555771e-2d63-5bd0-9820-b3496a00fcea', 'word_count': 308, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0555771e-2d63-5bd0-9820-b3496a00fcea'}, {'abstract': 'An American finance executive leaves behind her cushy life in favor of a musical career in this humdrum romance set in the Scottish Highlands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/30/movies/falling-for-figaro-review.html', 'snippet': 'An American finance executive leaves behind her cushy life in favor of a musical career in this humdrum romance set in the Scottish Highlands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I must admit it’s refreshing to see a plus-size woman not only nab the promotion and the hunky guy, but throw it all away within the first 15 minutes. Unfortunately, my plaudits for “Falling for Figaro” mostly end there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30falling-pix/merlin_195150480_581e3fa2-7b36-451a-859e-d2f1fd697826-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/20