': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2021/09/30/arts/music/classical-music-recordings.html', 'snippet': 'Haydn piano sonatas, a Shostakovich explosion and the fantastical opera “Sweet Land” are among the highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not all that long ago was a drearier time, when Haydn’s piano sonatas were taken less seriously than those of Mozart and Beethoven. That’s certainly not the case now, at least on record. Marc-André Hamelin brought out a wonderful selection on Hyperion around a decade ago, his brilliance tempered with elegance; Jean-Efflam Bavouzet’s ongoing survey on Chandos is one of the glories of the 21st-century record industry, nine volumes and counting of playing that is poised and polished, as well as ideally flamboyant and aptly witty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2021/09/30/arts/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid/30CLASSICAL-ALBUMS-Grid-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail'